%rec: default

# D1's speech, one record per _sfx_id: internal_name is the cue the game plays, text: what the line said in
# Diablo (reference/d1_voice_transcripts.tsv). No sound: means silent — assign one with ./remap_voices.sh.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH1
name: Adria: The dead who walk among the living follow the cursed king. He...
text: The dead who walk among the living follow the cursed king. He holds the power to raise yet more warriors for an ever-growing army of the undead. If you do not stop his reign, he will surely march across this land and slay all who still live here.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH2
name: Adria: No mortal can truly understand the mind of the demon. Never l...
text: No mortal can truly understand the mind of the demon. Never let their erratic actions confuse you, as that too may be their plan.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH3
name: Adria: I did not know this Lazarus of whom you speak, but I do sense...
text: I did not know this Lazarus of whom you speak, but I do sense a great conflict within his being. He poses a great danger and will stop at nothing to serve the powers of darkness which have claimed him as theirs.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH4
name: Adria: The people of Tristram will die if you cannot restore fresh w...
text: The people of Tristram will die if you cannot restore fresh water to their wells. Know this. Demons are at the heart of this matter, but they remain ignorant of what they have spawned.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH5
name: Adria: Seek out the domicile to which Pepin the Healer has directed...
text: Seek out the domicile to which Pepin the Healer has directed you. It is there that your missions will become clear and your methods evident.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH6
name: Adria: The succubus is a demon that feasts upon the essence of morta...
text: The succubus is a demon that feasts upon the essence of mortal men. You will find that Andariel has quite an appetite. The town will soon be devoid of any adult males unless you stop her feeding. Now.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH7
name: Adria: You will become an eternal servant of the Dark Lords should y...
text: You will become an eternal servant of the Dark Lords should you perish within this cursed domain. Enter the Chamber of Bone at your own peril.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH8
name: Adria: You must destroy the two demons that Horazon has trapped with...
text: You must destroy the two demons that Horazon has trapped within his sanctum at all costs. Should they escape from their imprisonment, they will create a link to this world that will make what lies below the cathedral seem like a children's tale.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH9
name: Adria: The once proud Iswal is trapped deep beneath the surface of t...
text: The once proud Iswal is trapped deep beneath the surface of this world. His honor stripped and his visage altered. He is trapped in immortal torment, charged to conceal the very thing that could free him.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH10
name: Adria: The butcher is a sadistic creature that delights in the tortu...
text: The butcher is a sadistic creature that delights in the torture and pain of others. You have seen his handiwork in the drunkard Farnham. His destruction will do much to ensure the safety of this village.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH11
name: Adria: The lair of the butcher is steeped in demonic power, and cast...
text: The lair of the butcher is steeped in demonic power, and casting any spell of passage there could cause unexpected results.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH12
name: Adria: This is a place of great anguish and terror, and so serves it...
text: This is a place of great anguish and terror, and so serves its master well. Tread carefully, or you may yourself be staying much longer than you had anticipated.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH13
name: Adria: You may meet people who are trapped within the Labyrinth, suc...
text: You may meet people who are trapped within the Labyrinth, such as Lachdanan. I sense in him honor and great guilt. Aid him, and you aid all of Tristram.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH14
name: Adria: There are many artifacts within the labyrinth that hold power...
text: There are many artifacts within the labyrinth that hold powers beyond the comprehension of mortals. Some of these hold fantastic power that can be used by either the light or the darkness. Securing the anvil from below could shift the course of the Sinnwar towards the light.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH15
name: Adria: Should you find these stones of blood, use them carefully. Th...
text: Should you find these stones of blood, use them carefully. The way is fraught with danger, and your only hope rests within your self-trust.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH16
name: Adria: This legendary place is real, and great rewards await you sho...
text: This legendary place is real, and great rewards await you should you find it. Nothing more can I say.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH17
name: Adria: You must be ever watchful, for Flesh Doom is an enemy who is...
text: You must be ever watchful, for Flesh Doom is an enemy who is both cruel and quick. His ebon blade is composed of the essence of evil. If you can destroy both of them, it would do much to weaken his dark master.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH18
name: Adria: His prowess with the blade is awesome, and he has lived for t...
text: His prowess with the blade is awesome, and he has lived for thousands of years knowing only warfare. I am sorry. I cannot see if you will defeat him.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH19
name: Adria: Maintain your quest. Finding a treasure that is lost is not e...
text: Maintain your quest. Finding a treasure that is lost is not easy. Finding a treasure that is hidden, less so. I will leave you with this. Do not let the sands of time confuse your search.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH20
name: Adria: The Heaven Stone is very powerful, and were it any but Griswo...
text: The Heaven Stone is very powerful, and were it any but Griswold who bid you find it, I would prevent it. He will harness its powers, and its use will be for the good of us all.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH21
name: Adria: Oh, I'm afraid this does not bode well at all. This map of th...
text: Oh, I'm afraid this does not bode well at all. This map of the stars portends great disaster, but its secrets are not mine to tell. The time has come for you to have a very serious conversation with the storyteller.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH22
name: Adria: What do we have here? Interesting. It looks like a book of re...
text: What do we have here? Interesting. It looks like a book of reagents. Keep your eyes open for a black mushroom. It should be fairly large and easy to identify. If you find it, bring it to me, won't you?

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH23
name: Adria: It's a big black mushroom that I need. Now run off and get it...
text: It's a big black mushroom that I need. Now run off and get it for me so that I can use it for a special concoction that I am working on.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH24
name: Adria: Yes, this will be perfect for a brew that I am creating. By t...
text: Yes, this will be perfect for a brew that I am creating. By the way, the healer is looking for the brain of some demon or another so he can treat those who have been afflicted by their poisonous venom. I believe that he intends to make an elixir from it. If you help him find what he needs, please see if you can get a sample of the elixir for me.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH25
name: Adria: Why have you brought that here? I have no need for a demon's...
text: Why have you brought that here? I have no need for a demon's brain at this time. I do need some of the elixir that the healer is working on. He needs that grotesque organ that you are holding. And then bring me the elixir. Simple when you think about it, isn't it?

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH26
name: Adria: What? Now you bring me that elixir from the healer? Oh, I was...
text: What? Now you bring me that elixir from the healer? Oh, I was able to finish my brew without it. Why don't you just keep it?

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH27
name: Adria: Hello, good friend. I have been working on a means to increas...
text: Hello, good friend. I have been working on a means to increase the strength of my potions. I believe that I could brew better potions if you could just find me the correct reagents.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH28
name: Adria: Remember, with the correct reagents, my potions are more powe...
text: Remember, with the correct reagents, my potions are more powerful.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH29
name: Adria: Excellent. Just a pinch should do it. Ah, here is a sample.
text: Excellent. Just a pinch should do it. Ah, here is a sample.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH30
name: Adria: It seems that there are many uses for the scrolls which are f...
text: It seems that there are many uses for the scrolls which are found beneath the church. I should be able to scribe a book of magic if I had enough of the proper scrolls to study.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH31
name: Adria: Remember, with enough scrolls, I can create a book of magic f...
text: Remember, with enough scrolls, I can create a book of magic for you.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH32
name: Adria: Yes, I can see that when I combine these scrolls just so, I w...
text: Yes, I can see that when I combine these scrolls just so, I will teach you what I have learned so that you may also know more secrets of this magic.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH33
name: Adria: I have a quest for you, if you are brave enough to accept it....
text: I have a quest for you, if you are brave enough to accept it. Great power can be found in some of the devices that may be hidden below the church. With the right ones, I could work wonders.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH34
name: Adria: Remember, the right device in my hands can become quite power...
text: Remember, the right device in my hands can become quite powerful.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH35
name: Adria: This is amazing. The mystic energies in this crystal are powe...
text: This is amazing. The mystic energies in this crystal are powerful, but unfocused. If you could find for me a specific staff to channel its power through...

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH36
name: Adria: The crystal holds a magic that is strong, but you need to fin...
text: The crystal holds a magic that is strong, but you need to find the correct staff with which to focus its energy.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH37
name: Adria: Hand me that staff and stand back. Vitate chlorum on dunium....
text: Hand me that staff and stand back. Vitate chlorum on dunium. It is complete.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH38
name: Adria: I sense a soul in search of answers.
text: I sense a soul in search of answers.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH39
name: Adria: Wisdom is earned, not given. If you discover a tome of knowle...
text: Wisdom is earned, not given. If you discover a tome of knowledge, devour its words. Should you already have knowledge of the arcane mysteries scribed within a book, remember that level of mastery can always increase.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH40
name: Adria: The greatest power is often the shortest lived. You may find...
text: The greatest power is often the shortest lived. You may find ancient words of power written upon scrolls of parchment. The strength of these scrolls lies in the ability of either apprentice or adept to cast them with equal ability. Their weakness is that they must first be read aloud and can never be kept at the ready in your mind. Use them with care.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH41
name: Adria: Though the heat of the sun is beyond measure, the mere flame...
text: Though the heat of the sun is beyond measure, the mere flame of a candle is of greater danger. No energies, no matter how great, can be used without the proper focus. For many spells, ensorcelled staves may be charged with magical energies many times over. I have the ability to restore their power, but know that nothing is done without a price.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH42
name: Adria: The sum of our knowledge is in the sum of its people. Should...
text: The sum of our knowledge is in the sum of its people. Should you find a book or scroll that you cannot decipher, do not hesitate to bring it to me. If I can make sense of it, I will share what I find.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH43
name: Adria: To a man who only knows iron, there is no greater magic than...
text: To a man who only knows iron, there is no greater magic than steel. The blacksmith Griswold is more of a sorcerer than he knows. His ability to meld fire and metal is unequaled in this land.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH44
name: Adria: Corruption has the strength of deceit, but innocence holds th...
text: Corruption has the strength of deceit, but innocence holds the power of purity. The young woman Jillian has a pure heart, placing the needs of her matriarch over her own. She fears me, but it is only because she does not understand me.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH45
name: Adria: A chest opened in darkness holds no greater treasure than whe...
text: A chest opened in darkness holds no greater treasure than when it is opened in the light. The storyteller Cain is an enigma, but only to those who do not look. His knowledge of what lies beneath the cathedral is far greater than even he allows himself to realize.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH46
name: Adria: The higher you place your faith in one man, the farther it ha...
text: The higher you place your faith in one man, the farther it has to fall. Farnam has lost his soul, but not to any demon. It was lost when he saw his fellow townspeople betrayed by the Archbishop Lazarus. He has knowledge to be gleaned, but you must separate fact from fantasy.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH47
name: Adria: The hand, the heart, and the mind can perform miracles when t...
text: The hand, the heart, and the mind can perform miracles when they are in perfect harmony. The healer Pepin sees into the body in a way that even I cannot. His ability to restore the sick and injured is magnified by his understanding of the creation of elixirs and potions. He is as great an ally as you have in Tristram.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH48
name: Adria: Faith is absolute belief in the unseen. The priest Tremaine i...
text: Faith is absolute belief in the unseen. The priest Tremaine is from a holy order long asleep in this land. He keeps a promise and a charge issued ages ago and sustains a union with realms that even my vision cannot reach. He knows much, but not as much as he believes.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH49
name: Adria: There is much about the future we cannot see, but when it com...
text: There is much about the future we cannot see, but when it comes, it will be the children who wield it. The boy word has a blackness upon his soul, but he poses no threat to the town or its people. His secretive dealings with the urchins and unspoken guilds of nearby towns gain him access to many devices that cannot be easily found in Tristram. It can provide assistance for your battle against the encroaching darkness.

internal_name: TSFX_WITCH50
name: Adria: Earth and walls and thatched canopy do not a home create. The...
text: Earth and walls and thatched canopy do not a home create. The innkeeper Ogden serves more of a purpose in this town than many understand. He provides shelter for Jillian and her matriarch, maintains what life Farnam has left to him, and provides an anchor for all who are left in the town to what Tristram once was. It is that memory that continues to feed their hopes for your success.

internal_name: USFX_LAZ1
name: Arch-Bishop Lazarus: Abandon your foolish quest. All that awaits you is the wrath...
text: Abandon your foolish quest. All that awaits you is the wrath of my master. You are too late to save the child. Now you will join him in hell.

internal_name: USFX_LAZ2
name: Arch-Bishop Lazarus: You are too late to save the child. Now you will join him in...
text: You are too late to save the child. Now you will join him in hell.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY0
name: Cain: The evil that you move against is the Dark Lord of Terror, kn...
text: The evil that you move against is the Dark Lord of Terror, known to mortal men as Diablo. It was he who was imprisoned within the labyrinth many centuries ago. Find Diablo, or we may never have a chance to rid the world of his evil again.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY1
name: Cain: Ah, the story of our king, is it? The tragic fall of Leoric w...
text: Ah, the story of our king, is it? The tragic fall of Leoric was a harsh blow to this land. The people always loved the king, and now they live in mortal fear of him. The question that I keep asking myself is how he could have fallen so far from the light, as Leoric had always been the holiest of men. Only the vilest powers of hell could so utterly destroy a man from within.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY2
name: Cain: I see that this strange behavior puzzles you as well. I would...
text: I see that this strange behavior puzzles you as well. I would surmise that since many demons fear the light of the sun and believe that it holds great power, it may be that the rising sun depicted on the sign you speak of has led them to believe that it too holds some arcane powers. Perhaps they are not all as smart as we had feared.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY3
name: Cain: Yes, you speak of Lazarus, one who was once well-respected in...
text: Yes, you speak of Lazarus, one who was once well-respected in our land. Even before King Leoric descended into madness and lost his son, the Archbishop Lazarus was acting strangely. Lazarus seemed to be motivated by unseen forces clinging to shadows and acting out some dark plan that was not his own.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY4
name: Cain: Hmm, I don't know what I can really tell you about this that...
text: Hmm, I don't know what I can really tell you about this that will be of any help. The water that fills our wells comes from an underground spring. I have heard of a tunnel that leads to a great lake. Perhaps they are one and the same. Unfortunately, I do not know what would cause our water supply to be tainted.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY5
name: Cain: Worms that rise up from the ground? Many of the ancient writi...
text: Worms that rise up from the ground? Many of the ancient writings speak of poisonous insects and foul creatures of the skies and seas plaguing mankind. It is no surprise that the very earth would offer up a similar peril now that the denizens of the underworld are upon us.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY6
name: Cain: While the barmaid may seem a bit confused at times, it is tru...
text: While the barmaid may seem a bit confused at times, it is true that men have been disappearing from the village. It reminds me of ancient writings about a demonic temptress called Andariel. Known as the Maiden of Anguish, her thirst for mortal blood was so great that she sought to learn a spell to breach the mortal realm. She took the knowledge she needed and so began to lure mortal men into her dark corner of hell. If these legends are true, she is not a creature to be taken lightly.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY7
name: Cain: A book that speaks of a chamber of human bones? Well, a chamb...
text: A book that speaks of a chamber of human bones? Well, a chamber of bone is mentioned in certain archaic writings that I studied in the libraries of the East. These tomes inferred that when the lords of the underworld desired to protect great treasures, they would create domains where those who died in the attempt to steal that treasure would be forever bound to defend it. but strangely fitting and...

internal_name: TSFX_STORY8
name: Cain: So, you seek knowledge concerning the wars of hell, do you? C...
text: So, you seek knowledge concerning the wars of hell, do you? Cryptic tomes speak of great battles that determine which of the demonic lords are to rule over hell. They also mention a bitter rivalry between two of these lords. Osmodon, who led the Horned Death against the Armies of Light, and Belial, known as the Lord of Lies. Their hatred of each other is eternal. For their loathing, lost even to themselves. Tales abound that the mad wizard Horazon somehow trapped the lieutenants of these two lords of hell within his sanctum. There can be no more dangerous a path to tread than the one that falls alongside of demons. Should you also seek this path, watch your life and your soul very carefully, my friend.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY9
name: Cain: Farnum has taken to drinking quite heavily since his encounte...
text: Farnum has taken to drinking quite heavily since his encounters in the labyrinth, but within the ramblings of this drunken man rests a legend well steeped in myth and mystery. Sit for a moment, my friend, and let me tell you of Iswal and Azurath. The saga of Iswal takes place during the lost battles in Hell. Iswal was an angel. Who was given charge of the holy rune blade, Azurath. Leading a daring assault on the Hellforge, Iswal was set upon by hundreds of blackened demons and was fatally wounded. The fiends cast the dying angel into a dark pit where the powers of chaos transformed him as he drowned in a whirlpool of burning blood. Evil possessed Iswal. The feathers of his wings burned away to reveal leathery skin and horns ripped through the flesh of his head. When he finally arose from that black pit, Iswal was an angel no more. Transformed into a creature of evil, he was once again given charge of Azurath, assuring that the blade would never again be used against the denizens of Hell.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY10
name: Cain: It seems that the Archbishop Lazarus goaded many of the towns...
text: It seems that the Archbishop Lazarus goaded many of the townsmen into venturing into the labyrinth to find the king's missing son. He played upon their fears and whipped them into a frenzied mob. None of them were prepared for what lay within the cold earth. Lazarus abandoned them down there, left in the clutches of unspeakable horrors, to die.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY11
name: Cain: You must have been speaking with Wirt. His is a sad story ind...
text: You must have been speaking with Wirt. His is a sad story indeed. That poor child was taken into the labyrinth by the demons, ripped from the very arms of his mother, Canus. May her soul rest in peace. The boy managed to escape, but only after they had chewed off his leg, and he has not been quite sane since. He often speaks in riddles, may hold some truth.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY12
name: Cain: You recite an interesting rhyme written in a style that remin...
text: You recite an interesting rhyme written in a style that reminds me of other works. Let me think now. What was it? Darkness shrouds the hidden, eyes glowing unseen, with only the sounds of razor claws briefly scraping to torment those poor souls who have been made sightless for all eternity. Calls of the Blind.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY13
name: Cain: You claim to have spoken with Lachdanen? He was a great hero...
text: You claim to have spoken with Lachdanen? He was a great hero during his life. Lachdanen was an honorable and just man who served his king faithfully for years. But of course you already know that. For those who were caught within the grasp of the king's curse, Lachdanen would be the least likely to submit to the darkness without a fight. So I suppose that your story could be true. If I were in your place, my friend, I would find a way to release him from his torture.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY14
name: Cain: Griswold speaks of the Anvil of Fury, a legendary artifact lo...
text: Griswold speaks of the Anvil of Fury, a legendary artifact long searched for, but never found. Crafted from the metallic bones of the razor-pit demons, the Anvil of Fury was smelt around the skulls of the five most powerful magi of the underworld. Carved with runes of power and chaos, any weapon or armor forged upon this anvil will be immersed into the realm of chaos. Embedding it with magical properties. It is said that the unpredictable nature of chaos makes it difficult to know what the outcome of this smithing will be.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY15
name: Cain: The Gateway of Blood and the Halls of Fire are landmarks of m...
text: The Gateway of Blood and the Halls of Fire are landmarks of mystic origin. Wherever this book you read from resides, it is surely a place of great power. Legends speak of a pedestal that is carved from obsidian stone and has a pool of boiling blood atop its bone-encrusted surface. There are also allusions to stones of blood that will open a door that guards an ancient treasure. The nature of this treasure is shrouded in speculation, my friend. But it is said that the ancient hero Arcane placed the holy armor Valor in a secret vault. Arcane was the first mortal to turn the tide of the Sinwar and chase the legions of darkness back to the burning hells. Just before Arcane died, his armor was hidden away in a secret vault. When this holy armor is again needed, a hero will arise to don Valor once more. Perhaps you are that hero.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY16
name: Cain: Hmm, an island where angels watched? Although Farnham's memor...
text: Hmm, an island where angels watched? Although Farnham's memory is often cloudy these days, that does seem familiar. Perhaps the ancient chronicles of the Sin War can help us. Ah, yes, here is something. In a time long forgotten, a sea of blue rested on the edge of a fiery netherworld. Angels and warriors of light could use this place to heal themselves and gather their strength. It was also a staging area where they could train and prepare for the Sin War. Legends speak of a trinity of rocks that hide the path to this island of the sunless sea.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY17
name: Cain: The priest Tremaine is a holy man from an ancient order. Thei...
text: The priest Tremaine is a holy man from an ancient order. Their dealings with the evil forces at work are well-respected and well-documented. I, too, have heard legends that speak of the cursed demon blade called Shadowfang. It is said to consume the tortured souls of its victims. These souls are trapped within its ebon blade and augment its unholy power. I have also read of a great hell-forge where even the mightiest weapon could be created or destroyed. Tread carefully when dealing with Shadowfang and its master, lest you be drawn into the sword as well.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY18
name: Cain: I know of only one legend that speaks of such a warrior as yo...
text: I know of only one legend that speaks of such a warrior as you describe. His story is found within the ancient chronicles of the Sin War. Stained by a thousand years of war, blood, and death, the Warlord of Blood stands upon a mountain of his tattered victims. His dark blade screams a black curse to the living, a tortured invitation to any who would stand before this execution. It is also written that although he was once a mortal who fought beside the Legion of Darkness during the Sin War, he lost his humanity to his insatiable hunger for blood.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY19
name: Cain: There was a time when this town was a frequent stop for trave...
text: There was a time when this town was a frequent stop for travelers from far and wide. Much has changed since then, but hidden caves and buried treasure are common fantasies of any child. Wirt seldom indulges in youthful games, so it may just be his imagination.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY20
name: Cain: Griswold speaks of the Heaven Stone that was destined for the...
text: Griswold speaks of the Heaven Stone that was destined for the Enclave located in the east. It was being taken there for further study. This stone glowed with an energy that somehow granted vision beyond that which a normal man could possess. I do not know what secrets it holds, my friend, but finding this stone would certainly prove most valuable.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY21
name: Cain: The witch, Adria, seeks a black mushroom? I know as much abou...
text: The witch, Adria, seeks a black mushroom? I know as much about black mushrooms as I do about red herrings. Perhaps Pepin the healer could tell you more. But this is something that cannot be found in any of my stories or books.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY22
name: Cain: So the legend of the map is real. Even I never truly believed...
text: So the legend of the map is real. Even I never truly believed any of it. I suppose it is time that I told you the truth about who I am, my friend. You see, I am not all that I seem. My true name is Deckard Cain, the Elder, and I am the last descendant of an ancient brotherhood that was dedicated to keeping and safeguarding the secrets of a timeless evil. An evil that quite obviously has now been released. The evil that you move against is the Dark Lord of Terror, known to mortal men as Diablo. It was he who was imprisoned within the labyrinth many centuries ago. The map that you hold now was created ages ago to mark the time when Diablo would rise again from his imprisonment. The stars on that map align. Diablo will be at the height of his power. He will be all but invincible. You are now in a race against time, my friend. Find Diablo and destroy him before the stars align. We may never have a chance to rid the world of his evil again.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY23
name: Cain: Our time is running short. I sense his dark power building, a...
text: Our time is running short. I sense his dark power building, and only you can stop him from attaining his full might.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY24
name: Cain: I'm sure that you tried your best, but I fear that even your...
text: I'm sure that you tried your best, but I fear that even your strength and will may not be enough. Diablo is now at the height of his earthly power, and you will need all your courage and strength to defeat him. May the light protect and guide you, my friend. I will help in any way that I am able.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY25
name: Cain: Hello, my friend. Stay a while and listen.
text: Hello, my friend. Stay a while and listen.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY26
name: Cain: While you are venturing deeper into the labyrinth, you may fi...
text: While you are venturing deeper into the labyrinth, you may find tomes of great knowledge hidden there. Read them carefully, for they can tell you things that even I cannot.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY27
name: Cain: I know of many myths and legends that may contain answers to...
text: I know of many myths and legends that may contain answers to questions that may arise in your journeys into the labyrinth. If you come across challenges and questions to which you seek knowledge, seek me out, and I will tell you what I can.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY28
name: Cain: "Griswold, a man of great action and great courage. I bet he...
text: "Griswold, a man of great action and great courage. I bet he never told you about the time he went into the labyrinth to save Wirt, did he? He knows his fair share of the dangers to be found there, but then again, so do you. He is a skilled craftsman, and if he claims to be able to help you in any way, you can count on his honesty and his skill."

internal_name: TSFX_STORY29
name: Cain: Ogden has owned and run the Rising Sun Inn and Tavern for alm...
text: Ogden has owned and run the Rising Sun Inn and Tavern for almost four years now. He purchased it just a few short months before everything here went to hell. He and his wife Garda do not have the money to leave as they invested all they had in making a life for themselves here. He is a good man with a deep sense of responsibility.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY30
name: Cain: Poor Farnum. He is a disquieting reminder of the doomed assem...
text: Poor Farnum. He is a disquieting reminder of the doomed assembly that entered into the cathedral with Lazarus on that dark day. He escaped with his life, but his courage and much of his sanity were left in some dark pit. He finds comfort only at the bottom of his tankard nowadays, but there are occasional bits of truth buried within his constant ramblings.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY31
name: Cain: The witch, Adria, is an anomaly here in Tristram. She arrived...
text: The witch, Adria, is an anomaly here in Tristram. She arrived shortly after the cathedral was desecrated, while most everyone else was fleeing. She had a small hut constructed at the edge of town, seemingly overnight, and has access to many strange and arcane artifacts and tomes of knowledge that even I have never seen before.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY32
name: Cain: Tremaine is an occasional visitor to our town and seems to ha...
text: Tremaine is an occasional visitor to our town and seems to have little problem coming and going. It is strange how at times anyone who tries to leave Tristram is hunted down and slain by the cloaked riders, and at other times it is a simple matter to leave. I think it is that uncertain fear that keeps some of us here, but we are glad for Tremaine's bravery and luck in keeping some contact with the rest of the kingdom. Thank you.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY33
name: Cain: The story of Wirt is a frightening and tragic one. He was tak...
text: The story of Wirt is a frightening and tragic one. He was taken from the arms of his mother and dragged into the labyrinth by the small, foul demons that wield wicked spears. There were many other children taken that day, including the son of King Leoric. The knights of the palace went below, but never returned. The blacksmith found the boy, but only after the foul beasts had begun to torture him for their sadistic pleasures.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY34
name: Cain: Ah, Pepin! I count him as a true friend, perhaps the closest...
text: Ah, Pepin! I count him as a true friend, perhaps the closest I have here. He is a bit addled at times, but never a more caring or considerate soul has existed. His knowledge and skills are equal by few, and his door is always open.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY35
name: Cain: Oh, Jillian is a fine woman, much adored for her high spirits...
text: Oh, Jillian is a fine woman, much adored for her high spirits and her quick laugh. She holds a special place in my heart. She stays on at the tavern to support her elderly grandmother who is too sick to travel. I sometimes fear for her safety, but I know that any man in the village would rather die than see her harmed.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY36
name: Cain: This does not bode well, for it confirms my darkest fears. Wh...
text: This does not bode well, for it confirms my darkest fears. While I did not allow myself to believe the ancient legends, I cannot deny them now. Perhaps the time has come to reveal who I am. My true name is Deckard Cain the Elder, and I am the last descendant of an ancient brotherhood that was dedicated to safeguarding the secrets of a timeless evil. An evil that quite obviously has now been released. The Archbishop Lazarus, once King Leoric's most trusted advisor, led a party of simple townsfolk into the labyrinth to find the king's missing son, Albrecht. Quite some time passed before they returned, and only a few of them escaped with their lives. Curse me for a fool! I should have suspected his veiled treachery then. It must have been Lazarus himself who kidnapped Albrecht and has since hidden him within the labyrinth. I do not understand why the Archbishop turned to the darkness, or what his interest is in the child, unless he means to sacrifice him to his dark masters. That must be what he has planned. The survivors of his rescue party say that Lazarus was last seen running into the deepest bowels of the labyrinth. and save the prince from the sacrificial blade of this demented fiend.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY37
name: Cain: You must hurry and rescue Albrecht from the hands of Lazarus....
text: You must hurry and rescue Albrecht from the hands of Lazarus. The prince and the people of this kingdom are counting on you.

internal_name: TSFX_STORY38
name: Cain: Your story is quite grim, my friend. Lazarus will surely burn...
text: Your story is quite grim, my friend. Lazarus will surely burn in hell for his horrific deed. The boy that you describe is not our prince. But I believe that Albrecht may yet be in danger. The symbol of power that you speak of must be a portal in the very heart of the labyrinth. Know this, my friend. The evil that you move against is the Dark Lord of Terror. He is known to mortal men... as Diablo. It was he who was imprisoned within the labyrinth many centuries ago. And I fear that he seeks to once again sow chaos in the realm of mankind. You must venture through the portal and destroy Diablo before it is too late.

internal_name: TSFX_COW1
name: Cow: *Mario grunts*
text: *Mario grunts*

internal_name: TSFX_COW2
name: Cow: Grrrr!
text: Grrrr!

internal_name: USFX_DIABLOD
name: Diablo: *Dramatic music*
text: *Dramatic music*

internal_name: PS_DIABLVLINT
name: Diablo: I'm your man, I shall pass over to you.
text: I'm your man, I shall pass over to you.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK1
name: Farnham: I don't care about that. Listen, no skeleton is gonna be my k...
text: I don't care about that. Listen, no skeleton is gonna be my king. Leoric is king. King! So you hear me? Hail to the king!

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK2
name: Farnham: You know what I think? Somebody took that sign, they're going...
text: You know what I think? Somebody took that sign, they're going to want lots of money for it. If I was Ogden, well, I'm not. But if I was, I'd just buy a new sign with some pretty drawing on it. Maybe a nice mug of ale or a piece of cheese.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK3
name: Farnham: They stab, then bite, then they're all around you. Liar! Liar...
text: They stab, then bite, then they're all around you. Liar! Liar! They're all dead. Dead! Do you hear me? They just keep falling and falling. The blood spilling out all over the floor. All his fault.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK4
name: Farnham: You drink water?
text: You drink water?

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK5
name: Farnham: Listen, listen. I don't even like worms. Don't tell me about...
text: Listen, listen. I don't even like worms. Don't tell me about your worms. I don't want your worms. Nope. No thanks. No worms for me.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK6
name: Farnham: Nom, nom, nom, nom, nom.
text: Nom, nom, nom, nom, nom.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK7
name: Farnham: Okay, so listen, there's this chamber of wood, see, and his w...
text: Okay, so listen, there's this chamber of wood, see, and his wife, you know, her, tells the tree, because she got away. Then I says that might work against him, but if you think I'm going to pay for this, you, yeah.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK8
name: Farnham: Sounds like a good idea to me. You better get started right a...
text: Sounds like a good idea to me. You better get started right away.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK9
name: Farnham: Did you ever hear the one with the canetails? I love that one.
text: Did you ever hear the one with the canetails? I love that one.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK10
name: Farnham: Big. Big Cleaver. Killing all my friends. Couldn't stab him....
text: Big. Big Cleaver. Killing all my friends. Couldn't stab him. Had to run away. Couldn't save them. Trapped in a room with so many bodies. So many friends. No!

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK11
name: Farnham: No, you can't let me go back there. I won't let you take me....
text: No, you can't let me go back there. I won't let you take me. Too much pain. Don't let you dead. Can't get the blood out of my eyes. My mouth.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK12
name: Farnham: Look here. That's pretty funny, huh? Get it? Blind? Look here.
text: Look here. That's pretty funny, huh? Get it? Blind? Look here.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK13
name: Farnham: Like Darren and it's dead. Everybody knows that. And you can'...
text: Like Darren and it's dead. Everybody knows that. And you can't fool me into thinking any other way. You can't talk to the dead. I know.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK14
name: Farnham: Griswold can't throw his anvil. What will he do then? And I'd...
text: Griswold can't throw his anvil. What will he do then? And I'd be angry, too, if someone took my anvil.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK15
name: Farnham: Hey, I'm here, I'm here, I'm here.
text: Hey, I'm here, I'm here, I'm here.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK16
name: Farnham: You're gonna hunt down a demon? Is that what you said? I know...
text: You're gonna hunt down a demon? Is that what you said? I know I didn't hear that. Cause nobody hunts down demons. Nope. Nobody.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK17
name: Farnham: Always you gotta talk about blood. What about flowers and sun...
text: Always you gotta talk about blood. What about flowers and sunshine? And that pretty girl that brings the drinks. Listen here, friend. You're obsessive, you know that?

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK18
name: Farnham: Hey, let me see that. Thanks.
text: Hey, let me see that. Thanks.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK19
name: Farnham: I used to have a nice ring. It was a really expensive one. Bl...
text: I used to have a nice ring. It was a really expensive one. Blue and green and red and silver. Don't remember what happened to it, though. I really miss that ring.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK20
name: Farnham: Ogden Mitt is a mean black mushroom, but I get sick if I drin...
text: Ogden Mitt is a mean black mushroom, but I get sick if I drink that. Listen, listen, here's the secret. Moderation is the key.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK21
name: Farnham: Listen here. Come close. I don't know if you know what I know...
text: Listen here. Come close. I don't know if you know what I know, but you have really got something here. That's a map.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK22
name: Farnham: Hey, you there. Come here, listen up. You know about the isla...
text: Hey, you there. Come here, listen up. You know about the island where angels watch? Pick the right rocks. But you better shield your eyes. Shield everything. I know, because I've been there and... Mm. Ale.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK23
name: Farnham: I want to tell you something, because I know all about this s...
text: I want to tell you something, because I know all about this stuff. It's my specialty. This here is the best. The best. That other of you ain't no good since I'm so stupid, dog.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK24
name: Farnham: No one ever listens to me. Somewhere, I ain't too sure, but s...
text: No one ever listens to me. Somewhere, I ain't too sure, but somewhere out of the church, a whole pile of gold gleaming, shining, just waiting for someone to get it.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK25
name: Farnham: I know you got your own ideas, and I know you're not going to...
text: I know you got your own ideas, and I know you're not going to believe this, but that weapon you got there, it just ain't no good against those big brutes. Oh, I don't care what Griswold says. They can't make anything like they used in the old days.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK26
name: Farnham: If I was you, and I ain't, but if I was, I'd sell all that st...
text: If I was you, and I ain't, but if I was, I'd sell all that stuff you got and get out of here. That boy out there, he's always got something good, but you gotta give him some gold, or he won't even show you what it's got.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK27
name: Farnham: Can't a fellow drink in peace?
text: Can't a fellow drink in peace?

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK28
name: Farnham: The guy who brings the drinks? Oh, yeah. What a pretty lady....
text: The guy who brings the drinks? Oh, yeah. What a pretty lady. So nice, too.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK29
name: Farnham: Why don't that old crumb do something for a change? Sure, sur...
text: Why don't that old crumb do something for a change? Sure, sure, she's got stuff. If you listen to me, she's unnatural. I ain't never seen her eat or drink. And you can't trust somebody who doesn't drink at least a little.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK30
name: Farnham: Kane isn't what he says he is. Sure, sure, he talks a good st...
text: Kane isn't what he says he is. Sure, sure, he talks a good story. Some of them are real scary or funny. But I think he knows more than he knows he knows.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK31
name: Farnham: Griswold? Good old Griswold. I love him like a brother. We fo...
text: Griswold? Good old Griswold. I love him like a brother. We fought together, you know, back when we... Lazarus. Lazarus. Lazarus!

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK32
name: Farnham: I like Pepper. He really tries, you know. Listen here. You sh...
text: I like Pepper. He really tries, you know. Listen here. You should make sure you get to know him. Good fellow like that with people always wanting help. Hey, I guess I'd be kind of like you, a hero. I was a hero, too, you know.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK33
name: Farnham: I have an elderly priest around here. If I did, I'd kick him...
text: I have an elderly priest around here. If I did, I'd kick him right in the... Can't even keep a church free of those hell spawned bastards. What good are they on? Those holy men. Liars. Liars!

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK34
name: Farnham: Word is a kid with more problems than even me. And I know all...
text: Word is a kid with more problems than even me. And I know all about problems. Listen here. That kid's got a sweet deal. He's been there, you know. Lost a leg. Gotta walk around on a piece of wood. So sad. So sad.

internal_name: TSFX_DRUNK35
name: Farnham: Ogden is the best man in town. I don't think his wife likes m...
text: Ogden is the best man in town. I don't think his wife likes me much, but as long as she keeps tapping kegs, I'll like her just fine. Seems like I've been spending more time with Ogden than most, but he's so good to me.

internal_name: USFX_GARBUD1
name: Gharbad the Weak: Please, no hurt, no kill. Keep alive, and next time, good bri...
text: Please, no hurt, no kill. Keep alive, and next time, good bring to you.

internal_name: USFX_GARBUD2
name: Gharbad the Weak: Something for you I am making. Again, not kill Garbod. Live a...
text: Something for you I am making. Again, not kill Garbod. Live and give good. You take this as proof I keep word.

internal_name: USFX_GARBUD3
name: Gharbad the Weak: Nothing yet. Almost done. Very powerful. Very strong. Live. L...
text: Nothing yet. Almost done. Very powerful. Very strong. Live. Live. No pain. And promise I keep.

internal_name: USFX_GARBUD4
name: Gharbad the Weak: This too good for you. Very powerful. You want, you take.
text: This too good for you. Very powerful. You want, you take.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID1
name: Gillian: I don't like to think about how the king died. I like to reme...
text: I don't like to think about how the king died. I like to remember him for the kind and just ruler that he was. His death was so sad and seemed very wrong somehow.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID2
name: Gillian: Oh my, is that where the sign went? My grandmother and I must...
text: Oh my, is that where the sign went? My grandmother and I must have slept right through the whole thing. Thank the light that those monsters didn't attack the inn.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID3
name: Gillian: I remember Lazarus as being a very kind and giving man. He sp...
text: I remember Lazarus as being a very kind and giving man. He spoke at my mother's funeral and was supportive of my grandmother and myself in a very troubled time. I pray every night that somehow he is still alive and safe.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID4
name: Gillian: My grandmother is very weak, and Garda says that we cannot dr...
text: My grandmother is very weak, and Garda says that we cannot drink the water from the wells. Please, can you do something to help us?

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID5
name: Gillian: Wait, before you say anything, my grandmother had a dream wit...
text: Wait, before you say anything, my grandmother had a dream with giant slithering creatures in it. She also saw Pepin running from a house in the town. Do you think this means anything?

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID6
name: Gillian: I'm afraid that I haven't heard anything about that. Perhaps...
text: I'm afraid that I haven't heard anything about that. Perhaps Cain the storyteller could be of some help.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID7
name: Gillian: This is something that is far beyond anything I have ever lea...
text: This is something that is far beyond anything I have ever learned. I can only think of one person in all of Tristram who could help you. Cain, of course.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID8
name: Gillian: When Farnham said something about a butcher killing people, I...
text: When Farnham said something about a butcher killing people, I immediately discounted it. But since you brought it up, maybe it is true.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID9
name: Gillian: How could you even think of going back to that place? What co...
text: How could you even think of going back to that place? What could be so important?

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID10
name: Gillian: If you have questions about blindness, you should talk to Pep...
text: If you have questions about blindness, you should talk to Pepin. I know that he gave my grandmother a potion that helped clear her vision, so maybe he can help you too.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID11
name: Gillian: I've never heard of a Lakhdanan before. Sorry, but I don't th...
text: I've never heard of a Lakhdanan before. Sorry, but I don't think that I can be of much help to you.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID12
name: Gillian: Griswold's father used to tell some of us when we were growin...
text: Griswold's father used to tell some of us when we were growing up about a giant anvil that was used to make mighty weapons. He said that when a hammer was struck upon this anvil, the ground would shake with a great fury. Whenever the earth moves, I always remember that story.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID13
name: Gillian: The story of the magic armor called Valor is something I ofte...
text: The story of the magic armor called Valor is something I often heard the boys talk about. You had better ask one of the men in the village.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID14
name: Gillian: Those are the words of a drunkard. I don't see how they could...
text: Those are the words of a drunkard. I don't see how they could be true.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID15
name: Gillian: I heard that the priest Tremaine was going to perform an exor...
text: I heard that the priest Tremaine was going to perform an exorcism, but I didn't go. I don't see why we all have to spend every moment captive to what is lurking underneath our town. I know that many have died at the hands of these monsters, but we need to try to go on. I know that you have come here to free Tristram from the clutches of darkness, and I hope that one day we can live in peace again.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID16
name: Gillian: If you are to battle such a fierce opponent, may Light be you...
text: If you are to battle such a fierce opponent, may Light be your guide and your defender. I will keep you in my thoughts.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID17
name: Gillian: A treasure map? Do you have it with you? Let me see. Hmm. It...
text: A treasure map? Do you have it with you? Let me see. Hmm. It looks like this is pretty old, and some of the buildings in the town are not on this map. Oh, I wish I could go and look for the treasure with you, but I have to start work soon.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID18
name: Gillian: Well, a caravan of some very important people did stop here,...
text: Well, a caravan of some very important people did stop here, but that was quite a while ago. They had strange accents and were starting on a long journey, as I recall. I don't see how you could hope to find anything that they would have been carrying.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID19
name: Gillian: I think Ogden might have some mushrooms in the storage cellar...
text: I think Ogden might have some mushrooms in the storage cellar. Why don't you ask him?

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID20
name: Gillian: The best person to ask about that sort of thing would be our...
text: The best person to ask about that sort of thing would be our storyteller. Cain is very knowledgeable about ancient writings, and that is easily the oldest-looking piece of paper that I have ever seen.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID21
name: Gillian: "'Beg pardon, but have you heard what has been happening? Som...
text: "'Beg pardon, but have you heard what has been happening? Some of the men have vanished from the village. Deesa's sons, Aeneas and Roof, claim to have seen strange lights glowing deep within the woods a few days ago, but no one has heard from them since. I, too, have seen a crimson shimmering from beyond the ash groves, but I have been too afraid to approach it. I fear that Ogden or our healer Pepin may be next. Won't you please find out what has happened?'

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID22
name: Gillian: Have you looked into what has caused those strange lights yet...
text: Have you looked into what has caused those strange lights yet? There are more men missing since last we spoke, and I'm beginning to fear that soon we may all vanish.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID23
name: Gillian: Demons that assume the form of beautiful women, you say? That...
text: Demons that assume the form of beautiful women, you say? That's horrible. Thank the light that you solved this mystery before any more of our men were lured to their deaths. Thank you for keeping us safe from the powers of darkness once again.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID24
name: Gillian: Pray your pardon, but I have something to tell you that you m...
text: Pray your pardon, but I have something to tell you that you may find interesting. It was the strangest thing. While drinking at the tavern, Farnum was rambling about something called Azurath. He also said something about a fallen angel. It was hard to understand him because he was very drunk and disoriented, but I seemed to remember something about a key in a barrel. He also kept covering his face and repeating the word Iswal over and over again.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID25
name: Gillian: You know, now that I think about it, maybe it wasn't a key in...
text: You know, now that I think about it, maybe it wasn't a key in a barrel, but a barrel that was the key. Does that make any more sense?

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID26
name: Gillian: Azurath and Izual. I don't know why I didn't remember that st...
text: Azurath and Izual. I don't know why I didn't remember that story earlier. I've heard it often enough from my grandmother and Cain the storyteller. Well, I hope that my information was still more of a help than a hindrance. May light guide you, my friend.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID27
name: Gillian: My grandmother often tells me stories about the strange force...
text: My grandmother often tells me stories about the strange forces that inhabit the graveyard outside of the church, and it may well interest you to hear one of them. She said that if you were to leave the proper offering in the cemetery, enter the cathedral to pray for the dead, and then return, the offering would be altered in some strange way. I don't know if this is just the talk of an old sick woman, but anything seems possible these days.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID28
name: Gillian: I know that my grandmother's story seems strange, but the gra...
text: I know that my grandmother's story seems strange, but the graveyard does have many mysteries surrounding it. It couldn't hurt you to put something there and see what happens, could it? Maybe you will find out something that will help us all.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID29
name: Gillian: My grandmother had a dream about you last night. She said tha...
text: My grandmother had a dream about you last night. She said that in her dream you used your bare hands to defeat one of those foul monsters that lurk under the church. When it died, it exploded into fabulous treasure. Although she was a bit frightened by her dream, she was able to describe the beast quite clearly to me.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID30
name: Gillian: My grandmother had that exact same dream again. She said you...
text: My grandmother had that exact same dream again. She said you were quite brave and seemed very pleased with your prize.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID31
name: Gillian: Good day. How may I serve you?
text: Good day. How may I serve you?

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID32
name: Gillian: My grandmother had a dream that you would come and talk to me...
text: My grandmother had a dream that you would come and talk to me. She has visions, you know, and can see into the future.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID33
name: Gillian: The woman at the edge of town is a witch. She seems nice enou...
text: The woman at the edge of town is a witch. She seems nice enough and her name Adria is very pleasing to the ear, but I'm very afraid of her. It would take someone quite brave like you to see what she is doing out there.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID34
name: Gillian: Our blacksmith is a point of pride to the people of Tristram....
text: Our blacksmith is a point of pride to the people of Tristram. Not only is he a master craftsman who has won many contests within his guild, but he received praises from our King Leoric himself. May his soul rest in peace. Griswold is also a great hero. Just ask Cain.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID35
name: Gillian: Cain has been the storyteller of Tristram for as long as I ca...
text: Cain has been the storyteller of Tristram for as long as I can remember. He knows so much and can tell you just about anything, about almost everything.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID36
name: Gillian: Farnam is a drunkard who fills his belly with ale and everyon...
text: Farnam is a drunkard who fills his belly with ale and everyone else's ears with nonsense. I know that both Pepin and Ogden feel sympathy for him, but I get so frustrated watching him slip farther and farther into a befuddled stupor every night.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID37
name: Gillian: Pepin saved my grandmother's life, and I know that I can neve...
text: Pepin saved my grandmother's life, and I know that I can never repay him for that. His ability to heal any sickness is more powerful than the mightiest sword and more mysterious than any spell you can name. If you ever are in need of healing, Pepin can help you.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID38
name: Gillian: i really don't know much about the priest remain he never vis...
text: i really don't know much about the priest remain he never visits the tavern preferring to keep to the company of pepin and cain perhaps it is because they too have more scholarly pursuits

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID39
name: Gillian: I grew up with Wirt's mother, Canis. Although she was only sl...
text: I grew up with Wirt's mother, Canis. Although she was only slightly hurt when those hideous creatures stole him, she never recovered. I think she died of a broken heart. Wirt has become a mean-spirited youngster, looking only to profit from the sweat of others. I know that he suffered and has seen horrors that I cannot even imagine. But some of that darkness hangs over him still.

internal_name: TSFX_BMAID40
name: Gillian: Ogden and his wife have taken me and my grandmother into thei...
text: Ogden and his wife have taken me and my grandmother into their home and have even let me earn a few gold pieces by working at the inn. I owe so much to them and hope one day to leave this place and help them start a grand hotel in the east.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH1
name: Griswold: I made many of the weapons and most of the armor that King Le...
text: I made many of the weapons and most of the armor that King Leoric used to outfit his knights. I even crafted a huge two-handed sword of the finest mithril for him, as well as a field crown to match. I still can't believe how he died, but it must have been some sinister force that drove him insane.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH2
name: Griswold: Demons stole Ogden's sign, you say? That doesn't sound much l...
text: Demons stole Ogden's sign, you say? That doesn't sound much like the atrocities I've heard of or seen. Demons are concerned with ripping out your heart, not your signpost.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH3
name: Griswold: Ah, I was there when Lazarus led us into the labyrinth. He sp...
text: Ah, I was there when Lazarus led us into the labyrinth. He spoke of holy retribution. But when we started fighting those hellspawn, he did not so much as lift his mace against them. He just ran deeper into the dim, endless chambers that were filled with the servants of darkness.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH4
name: Griswold: Pippin has told you the truth. We will need fresh water badly...
text: Pippin has told you the truth. We will need fresh water badly, and soon. I've tried to clear one of the smaller wells, but it reeks of stagnant filth. It must be getting clogged at the source.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH5
name: Griswold: I've seen no such things in my shop, but I will keep a close...
text: I've seen no such things in my shop, but I will keep a close watch for them. Perhaps if they come this way, they won't take kindly to the fires of my forge.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH6
name: Griswold: I admit that I too have seen these strange lights, but I have...
text: I admit that I too have seen these strange lights, but I have not felt pulled towards them. I'll be sure to steer clear of them, and will tell everyone that visits here to do likewise.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH7
name: Griswold: Ach, no, nothing of this place. But you may try asking Cain....
text: Ach, no, nothing of this place. But you may try asking Cain. He talks about many things, and we're not surprised maybe he had some answers to your question.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH8
name: Griswold: A bold tale indeed. My limited time beneath the cathedral lea...
text: A bold tale indeed. My limited time beneath the cathedral leaves me purely equipped to offer you any help with this. But, as always, you'll find Cain well versed in legends and folklore.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH9
name: Griswold: The blade Azurath, oh, it's legend. It was cast by the angeli...
text: The blade Azurath, oh, it's legend. It was cast by the angelic weaponsmith, Synedade, and tempered within the fires of judgment. Whoever wields this weapon will find the legions of hell at his feet. If you found this blade, I would begin to truly believe that you can end the nightmare that has befallen our town.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH10
name: Griswold: I saw what Furnum calls the butcher as it swathed a path thro...
text: I saw what Furnum calls the butcher as it swathed a path through the bodies of my friends. He swung a cleaver as large as an axe, hewing limbs and cutting down brave men where they stood. I was separated from the fray by a host of small screeching demons and somehow found the stairway leading out. I never saw that hideous beast again, but his bloodstained visage haunts me to this day.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH11
name: Griswold: When I found Wirt, he was very near a room that sounds like t...
text: When I found Wirt, he was very near a room that sounds like the vile pitch I've described. The stench of death was heavy in the air and consumed as I was with getting the lad to safety. I did not go further than I had to. If he claims to know something of that place, I would not discount his word easily.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH12
name: Griswold: I'm afraid that I've neither heard nor seen a place that matc...
text: I'm afraid that I've neither heard nor seen a place that matches your vivid description, my friend. Perhaps Cain the Storyteller could be of some help.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH13
name: Griswold: If it is actually Lachdanon that you've met, then I would adv...
text: If it is actually Lachdanon that you've met, then I would advise that you aid him. I dealt with him on several occasions and found him to be honest and loyal in nature. The curse that fell upon the followers of King Lyoric would fall especially hard upon him.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH14
name: Griswold: The armor known as Valor could be what tips the scales in you...
text: The armor known as Valor could be what tips the scales in your favor. I'll tell you that many have looked for it, including myself. Arcane hid it well, my friend, and it'll take more than a bit of luck to unlock the secrets that have kept it concealed, oh, lo, these many years.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH15
name: Griswold: Farnham speaks of a place that exists, at least in legend. Wa...
text: Farnham speaks of a place that exists, at least in legend. Warriors would go to a place at the edge of hell to gird themselves for battle against the armies of darkness. If the stories are true, untold treasures could lie upon this island of the sunless sea.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH16
name: Griswold: Ah, you speak of an ancient and evil weapon. Tread lightly in...
text: Ah, you speak of an ancient and evil weapon. Tread lightly in this area. The legends of Shadowfang are as black as a moonless winter night. Crafted within the Hellforge, Shadowfang can rend the very soul from whoever it strikes. Ah, I do not envy you if it is in your mind to defeat the one who wields it. May light protect you, brave hero.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH17
name: Griswold: Dark and wicked legend surrounds the one warlord of blood. Be...
text: Dark and wicked legend surrounds the one warlord of blood. Be well prepared, my friend, for he shows no mercy or quarter.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH18
name: Griswold: A what? This is foolishness. There's no treasure buried here...
text: A what? This is foolishness. There's no treasure buried here in Tristram. Let me see that. Look, these drawings are inaccurate. They don't match our town at all. I'd keep my mind on what lies below the cathedral and not what lies below our topsoil.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH19
name: Griswold: If Adria doesn't have one of these, I can bet that's a rare t...
text: If Adria doesn't have one of these, I can bet that's a rare thing indeed. I can offer you no more help than that. But that sounds like a huge, gargantuan, swollen, bloated mushroom. Well, good hunting, I suppose.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH20
name: Griswold: I've never seen a map of this sort before. Where'd you get it...
text: I've never seen a map of this sort before. Where'd you get it? Ugh, although I have no idea how to read this, Cain or Adrian may be able to provide the answers that you seek.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH21
name: Griswold: Greetings! It's always a pleasure to see one of my best custo...
text: Greetings! It's always a pleasure to see one of my best customers. I know that you've been venturing deeper into the labyrinth, and there's a story I was told that you may find worth the time to listen to. One of the men who returned from the labyrinth told me about a mystic anvil that he came across during his escape. His description reminded me of legends I had heard in my youth about the burning Hellforge, where powerful weapons of magic are crafted. The legend had it that deep within the Hellforge rested the Anvil of Fury. This anvil contained within it the very essence of the demonic underworld. It is said that any weapon crafted upon the burning anvil is imbued with great power. If this anvil is indeed the Anvil of Fury, I may be able to make you a weapon capable of defeating even the darkest lord of hell. Find the anvil for me, and I'll get to work.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH22
name: Griswold: Nothing yet, eh? Well, keep searching. A whipping force upon...
text: Nothing yet, eh? Well, keep searching. A whipping force upon the anvil could be your best hope. And I'm sure that I can make you one of legendary proportions.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH23
name: Griswold: Oh, I can hardly believe it. This is the Anvil of Fury. Good...
text: Oh, I can hardly believe it. This is the Anvil of Fury. Good work, my friend. Now, we'll show those bastards that there are no weapons in hell more deadly than those made by men. Take this, and may light protect you.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH24
name: Griswold: Stay for a moment. I have a story you might find interesting....
text: Stay for a moment. I have a story you might find interesting. A caravan that was bound for the Eastern Kingdoms passed through here some time ago. It was supposedly carrying a piece of the heavens that had fallen to Earth. The caravan was ambushed by cloaked riders just north of here along the roadway. I searched the wreckage for this sky rock, but it was nowhere to be found. If you should find it, I believe that I can fashion something useful from it.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH25
name: Griswold: I'm still waiting for you to bring me that stone from the hea...
text: I'm still waiting for you to bring me that stone from the heavens. I know that I can make something powerful out of it.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH26
name: Griswold: Let me see that. Aye, aye, it is as I believed. Give me a mom...
text: Let me see that. Aye, aye, it is as I believed. Give me a moment. Ah, here you are. I arranged pieces of the stone within a silver ring that my father left me. Ah, I hope it serves you well.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH27
name: Griswold: I'm in luck! A caravan has stopped just outside the village a...
text: I'm in luck! A caravan has stopped just outside the village and has taken supplies to the lands of the east. Certain items will bring a special price, if you can get them for me.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH28
name: Griswold: We can both turn a nice profit if he can deliver the right go...
text: We can both turn a nice profit if he can deliver the right goods to me. What do you say?

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH29
name: Griswold: Ah, you're just in time. The caravan is leaving tonight. Here...
text: Ah, you're just in time. The caravan is leaving tonight. Here is your cut, friend.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH30
name: Griswold: I believe that I may have found a way to greatly improve some...
text: I believe that I may have found a way to greatly improve some weapons. If you can bring me what I need, I'd be willing to try out my idea. And if it works, it's yours.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH31
name: Griswold: I still think I can improve the right weapon!
text: I still think I can improve the right weapon!

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH32
name: Griswold: Let me just do this, and this, and this. Ah, it works! Take t...
text: Let me just do this, and this, and this. Ah, it works! Take this back and give it a try.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH33
name: Griswold: I'm working on a method for strengthening armor. Unfortunatel...
text: I'm working on a method for strengthening armor. Unfortunately, I don't have what I need just now. If you could possibly bring me what I require, the first one is yours.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH34
name: Griswold: I still think I can strengthen the right armor. You know what...
text: I still think I can strengthen the right armor. You know what you need to bring me.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH35
name: Griswold: Good find! See if this works any better for you.
text: Good find! See if this works any better for you.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH36
name: Griswold: If you come across any enchanted equipment, I could try to le...
text: If you come across any enchanted equipment, I could try to learn how it was crafted and then use those methods for my own creations. I should probably start with something easy.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH37
name: Griswold: I still think that I can strip the knowledge of enchantments...
text: I still think that I can strip the knowledge of enchantments if you bring me a certain item.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH38
name: Griswold: Thank you, oh great and mighty customer, uh, uh, champion. Th...
text: Thank you, oh great and mighty customer, uh, uh, champion. This will take some study. Done.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH39
name: Griswold: Keep your eyes open for a figurine made of iron. I have uncov...
text: Keep your eyes open for a figurine made of iron. I have uncovered some old records concerning a specific type of figurine and the secrets of metal crafting that it holds.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH40
name: Griswold: I know that the right figurine could be quite powerful. If yo...
text: I know that the right figurine could be quite powerful. If you see what I'm looking for, get it and bring it to me straight away.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH41
name: Griswold: Oh, the secrets of this metal are fantastic! Oh, how I could...
text: Oh, the secrets of this metal are fantastic! Oh, how I could make the right item gleam with power!

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH42
name: Griswold: If you deliver to me the right item so I can combine it with...
text: If you deliver to me the right item so I can combine it with this metal, I could craft something worthy of the warriors of heaven!

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH43
name: Griswold: Your efforts are not in vain. It seems that all is as I had h...
text: Your efforts are not in vain. It seems that all is as I had hoped. I trust you will find this useful in your battles below?

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH44
name: Griswold: Whoa, what can I do for you?
text: Whoa, what can I do for you?

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH45
name: Griswold: If you're looking for a good weapon, let me show this to you....
text: If you're looking for a good weapon, let me show this to you. Take your basic blunt weapon, such as a mace. Works like a charm against most of those undying horrors down there. And there's nothing better to shatter skinny little skeletons.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH46
name: Griswold: The axe? Aye, that's a good weapon. Balanced against any foe....
text: The axe? Aye, that's a good weapon. Balanced against any foe. Look how it cleaves the air. And then imagine a nice fat demon head in its path. Keep in mind, however, that it is slow to swing. But talk about dealing a heavy blow!

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH47
name: Griswold: Look at that edge, that balance! A sword in the right hands,...
text: Look at that edge, that balance! A sword in the right hands, and against the right foe, is the master of all weapons! Its keen blade finds little to hack or pierce on the undead, but against a living, breathing enemy, a sword will bitter slice their flesh!

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH48
name: Griswold: Your weapons and armor will show the signs of your struggles...
text: Your weapons and armor will show the signs of your struggles against the darkness. If you bring them to me, with a bit of work and a hot forge, I can restore them to top fighting form.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH49
name: Griswold: while I have to practically smuggle in the metals and tools I...
text: while I have to practically smuggle in the metals and tools I need from caravans that skirt the edges of our damned town. That witch, Adria, always seems to get whatever she needs. If I knew even the smallest bit about how to harness magic as she did, I could make some truly incredible things.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH50
name: Griswold: Oh, Jillian is a nice lass. Shame that her gammer is in such...
text: Oh, Jillian is a nice lass. Shame that her gammer is in such poor health, or I would arrange to get both of them out of here on one of the trading caravans.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH51
name: Griswold: Sometimes I think that Cain talks too much, but I guess that'...
text: Sometimes I think that Cain talks too much, but I guess that's his calling in life. If I can bend steel as well as he can bend your ear, I can make a suit of court plate good enough for an emperor.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH52
name: Griswold: I was with Farnum that night that Lazarus led us into the lab...
text: I was with Farnum that night that Lazarus led us into the labyrinth. I never saw the Archbishop again, and I may not have survived if Farnum was not at my side. I fear that the attack left his soul as crippled as, well, another did my leg. I cannot fight this battle for him now. But I would if I could.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH53
name: Griswold: A good man who puts the needs of others above his own. You wo...
text: A good man who puts the needs of others above his own. You won't find anyone left in Tristram, or anyone else for that matter, who has a bad thing to say about the healer.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH54
name: Griswold: The priest, Tremaine, he's a solitary fellow who has no time...
text: The priest, Tremaine, he's a solitary fellow who has no time for most of us. He seems to prefer the company of Pepin or Cain. That's fine by me. I respect his passion and his commitment to his order, but I've no time for his prattling.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH55
name: Griswold: That lad is gonna get himself into serious trouble. Or I gues...
text: That lad is gonna get himself into serious trouble. Or I guess I should say, again. I've tried to interest him in working here and learning an honest trade. But he prefers the high profits of dealing in goods of devious origin. I kinda hold that against him after what happened to him. But I do wish he would at least be careful.

internal_name: TSFX_SMITH56
name: Griswold: The innkeeper has little business and no real way of turning...
text: The innkeeper has little business and no real way of turning a profit. He manages to make inns meet by providing food and lodging for those who occasionally drift through the village, but they're as likely to sneak off into the night as they are to pay him. If it weren't for the stores of grains and dried meats he kept in his cellar, why most of us would have starved during that first year when the entire countryside was overrun by demons.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE1
name: Hero: Rogue: Beyond the Hall of Heroes lies the Chamber of Bone. Eternal d...
text: Beyond the Hall of Heroes lies the Chamber of Bone. Eternal death awaits any who would seek to steal the treasures secured within this room. So speaks the Lord of Terror, and so it is written.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE2
name: Hero: Rogue: Let this tome serve as your warning. This is a forbidden plac...
text: Let this tome serve as your warning. This is a forbidden place. Return from whence you came and your life will be spared. Horazon, master of the disciplines that summon and bind creatures to this plane, promises death to those who pass beyond the five pillars. You have been admonished.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE3
name: Hero: Rogue: Then by binding the spirit to the crafted rock, it is given l...
text: Then by binding the spirit to the crafted rock, it is given life. Sounds like a spell of some kind.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE4
name: Hero: Rogue: The Creature of Flame by Horazon. Should be interesting reading.
text: The Creature of Flame by Horazon. Should be interesting reading.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE5
name: Hero: Rogue: Morta Vespa, Gaia Inumino, Evegin Jatan Luagratan.
text: Morta Vespa, Gaia Inumino, Evegin Jatan Luagratan.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE6
name: Hero: Rogue: The lieutenant of Belial is known as Grimspike. Beware this d...
text: The lieutenant of Belial is known as Grimspike. Beware this demon, for his strength appears immeasurable. Reading the scroll, and therefore speaking his name, near an arcane circle of binding will surely summon him there. Hmm, near a circle of binding, eh?

internal_name: PS_ROGUE7
name: Hero: Rogue: It seems that I may have brought something into this plane th...
text: It seems that I may have brought something into this plane that even I cannot control. The creature that fell into my astral trap is a very deadly demon. I've been able to bind it at the bottom of a pit, but it kills everything that I've sent there in attempts to defeat it. While it cannot escape, it does block the tunnels that lead to my protected haven. I am tempted to use the switch to open the tunnels to see if it will just leave, sir, demons I have trapped before. If I could just lure it somewhere else.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE8
name: Hero: Rogue: Your death will be avenged.
text: Your death will be avenged.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE9
name: Hero: Rogue: Rest in peace, my friend.
text: Rest in peace, my friend.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE10
name: Hero: Rogue: And so, locked beyond the gateway of blood and past the hall...
text: And so, locked beyond the gateway of blood and past the hall of fire, valor awaits for the hero of light to awaken.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE11
name: Hero: Rogue: I can see what you see not. Vision milky, then eyes rot. When...
text: I can see what you see not. Vision milky, then eyes rot. When you turn, they will be gone, whispering their hidden song. Then you see what cannot be. Shadows move where light should be. Out of darkness, out of mind, cast down into the halls of the blind.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE12
name: Hero: Rogue: The armories of hell are home to the warlord of blood. In his...
text: The armories of hell are home to the warlord of blood. In his wake lay the mutilated bodies of thousands. Angels and man alike have been cut down to fulfill his endless sacrifices to the dark ones, who scream for one thing, blood.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE13
name: Hero: Rogue: I can't use this yet.
text: I can't use this yet.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE14
name: Hero: Rogue: I can't carry anymore.
text: I can't carry anymore.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE15
name: Hero: Rogue: I have no room.
text: I have no room.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE16
name: Hero: Rogue: Now where would I put this?
text: Now where would I put this?

internal_name: PS_ROGUE17
name: Hero: Rogue: No way.
text: No way.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE18
name: Hero: Rogue: Not a chance.
text: Not a chance.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE19
name: Hero: Rogue: I would never use this.
text: I would never use this.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE20
name: Hero: Rogue: I'd have to equip that.
text: I'd have to equip that.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE21
name: Hero: Rogue: I can't move this.
text: I can't move this.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE22
name: Hero: Rogue: I can't move this, yet.
text: I can't move this, yet.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE23
name: Hero: Rogue: I can't open this.
text: I can't open this.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE24
name: Hero: Rogue: I can't open this, yet.
text: I can't open this, yet.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE25
name: Hero: Rogue: I can't lift this.
text: I can't lift this.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE26
name: Hero: Rogue: I can't lift this, yet.
text: I can't lift this, yet.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE27
name: Hero: Rogue: I can't cast that here.
text: I can't cast that here.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE28
name: Hero: Rogue: I can't cast that. Yet.
text: I can't cast that. Yet.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE29
name: Hero: Rogue: That didn't do anything.
text: That didn't do anything.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE30
name: Hero: Rogue: I can already do that.
text: I can already do that.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE31
name: Hero: Rogue: I don't need that.
text: I don't need that.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE32
name: Hero: Rogue: I don't need to do that.
text: I don't need to do that.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE33
name: Hero: Rogue: I don't want that.
text: I don't want that.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE34
name: Hero: Rogue: I don't have a spell ready.
text: I don't have a spell ready.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE35
name: Hero: Rogue: Not enough manna.
text: Not enough manna.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE36
name: Hero: Rogue: That would kill me.
text: That would kill me.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE37
name: Hero: Rogue: I can't do that.
text: I can't do that.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE38
name: Hero: Rogue: No.
text: No.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE39
name: Hero: Rogue: Yes!
text: Yes!

internal_name: PS_ROGUE40
name: Hero: Rogue: That won't work.
text: That won't work.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE41
name: Hero: Rogue: That won't work here.
text: That won't work here.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE42
name: Hero: Rogue: That won't work yet.
text: That won't work yet.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE43
name: Hero: Rogue: I can't get there from here.
text: I can't get there from here.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE44
name: Hero: Rogue: It's too heavy.
text: It's too heavy.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE45
name: Hero: Rogue: That's too big.
text: That's too big.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE46
name: Hero: Rogue: Ah, just what I was looking for.
text: Ah, just what I was looking for.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE47
name: Hero: Rogue: I've got a bad feeling about this.
text: I've got a bad feeling about this.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE48
name: Hero: Rogue: Got milk?
text: Got milk?

internal_name: PS_ROGUE49
name: Hero: Rogue: I'm not thirsty.
text: I'm not thirsty.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE50
name: Hero: Rogue: Hey, I'm no milkmaid.
text: Hey, I'm no milkmaid.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE51
name: Hero: Rogue: Hey, I could blow up the whole village.
text: Hey, I could blow up the whole village.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE52
name: Hero: Rogue: Yep, that's a cow, all right.
text: Yep, that's a cow, all right.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE53
name: Hero: Rogue: Too... heavy.
text: Too... heavy.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE54
name: Hero: Rogue: In spiritu sanctum.
text: In spiritu sanctum.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE55
name: Hero: Rogue: Predictum Otium.
text: Predictum Otium.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE56
name: Hero: Rogue: Ephesio orbitus ut inimicus.
text: Ephesio orbitus ut inimicus.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE57
name: Hero: Rogue: The enchantment is gone.
text: The enchantment is gone.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE58
name: Hero: Rogue: All too easy.
text: All too easy.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE59
name: Hero: Rogue: Back to the grave.
text: Back to the grave.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE60
name: Hero: Rogue: Time to die.
text: Time to die.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE61
name: Hero: Rogue: I'm not impressed.
text: I'm not impressed.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE62
name: Hero: Rogue: I'm sorry. Did I break your concentration?
text: I'm sorry. Did I break your concentration?

internal_name: PS_ROGUE63
name: Hero: Rogue: Vengeance is mine.
text: Vengeance is mine.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE64
name: Hero: Rogue: Die.
text: Die.

internal_name: PS_ROGUE65
name: Hero: Rogue: Yeah.
text: Yeah.

