internal_name: PS_WARR1
name: Hero: Warrior: Beyond the Hall of Heroes lies the Chamber of Bone. Eternal d...
text: Beyond the Hall of Heroes lies the Chamber of Bone. Eternal death awaits any who would seek to steal the treasures secured within this room. So speaks the Lord of Terror, and so it is written.

internal_name: PS_WARR2
name: Hero: Warrior: Let this tome serve as your warning. This is a forbidden plac...
text: Let this tome serve as your warning. This is a forbidden place. Return from whence you came and your life will be spared. Horazon, master of the disciplines that summon and bind creatures to this plane, promises death to those who pass beyond the five pillars. You have been admonished.

internal_name: PS_WARR3
name: Hero: Warrior: Then, by binding the spirit to the crafted rock, it is given...
text: Then, by binding the spirit to the crafted rock, it is given life. This sounds like a spell of some kind.

internal_name: PS_WARR4
name: Hero: Warrior: The Creature of Flame by Horazon. Should be interesting reading.
text: The Creature of Flame by Horazon. Should be interesting reading.

internal_name: PS_WARR5
name: Hero: Warrior: Morta, Vespa, Gaia, Innumino. Evegin, Jatan, Lua, Gretan.
text: Morta, Vespa, Gaia, Innumino. Evegin, Jatan, Lua, Gretan.

internal_name: PS_WARR6
name: Hero: Warrior: The lieutenant of Belial is known as Grimspike. Beware this d...
text: The lieutenant of Belial is known as Grimspike. Beware this demon, for his strength appears immeasurable. Reading this scroll and therefore speaking his name near an arcane circle of binding will surely summon him there. Hmm. Near a circle of binding.

internal_name: PS_WARR7
name: Hero: Warrior: This looks like some sort of journal. It seems that I may hav...
text: This looks like some sort of journal. It seems that I may have brought something to this plane that even I cannot control. The creature that fell into my astral trap is a very deadly demon. I have been able to bind it at the bottom of a pit, but it kills everything that I have sent there in attempts to defeat it. While it cannot escape, it does block the tunnels that lead to my protected haven. I am tempted to use the switch to open the tunnels to see if it will just leave, but I fear it is smarter than most of the lesser demons I have trapped before. If I could just lure it somewhere else.

internal_name: PS_WARR8
name: Hero: Warrior: Your death will be avenged.
text: Your death will be avenged.

internal_name: PS_WARR9
