text: I don't need to do that.

internal_name: PS_WARR33
name: Hero: Warrior: I don't want that.
text: I don't want that.

internal_name: PS_WARR34
name: Hero: Warrior: I don't have a spell ready.
text: I don't have a spell ready.

internal_name: PS_WARR35
name: Hero: Warrior: Not enough manna.
text: Not enough manna.

internal_name: PS_WARR36
name: Hero: Warrior: That would kill me.
text: That would kill me.

internal_name: PS_WARR37
name: Hero: Warrior: I can't do that.
text: I can't do that.

internal_name: PS_WARR38
name: Hero: Warrior: No.
text: No.

internal_name: PS_WARR39
name: Hero: Warrior: Yes.
text: Yes.

internal_name: PS_WARR40
name: Hero: Warrior: That won't work.
text: That won't work.

internal_name: PS_WARR41
name: Hero: Warrior: That won't work here.
text: That won't work here.

internal_name: PS_WARR42
name: Hero: Warrior: That won't work yet.
text: That won't work yet.

internal_name: PS_WARR43
name: Hero: Warrior: I can't get there from here.
text: I can't get there from here.

internal_name: PS_WARR44
name: Hero: Warrior: It's too heavy.
text: It's too heavy.

internal_name: PS_WARR45
name: Hero: Warrior: It's too big.
text: It's too big.

internal_name: PS_WARR46
name: Hero: Warrior: Just what I was looking for.
text: Just what I was looking for.

internal_name: PS_WARR47
name: Hero: Warrior: I've got a bad feeling about this.
text: I've got a bad feeling about this.

internal_name: PS_WARR48
name: Hero: Warrior: Got milk?
text: Got milk?

internal_name: PS_WARR49
name: Hero: Warrior: I'm not thirsty.
text: I'm not thirsty.

internal_name: PS_WARR50
name: Hero: Warrior: I'm no milkmaid.
text: I'm no milkmaid.

internal_name: PS_WARR51
name: Hero: Warrior: I could blow up the whole village.
text: I could blow up the whole village.

internal_name: PS_WARR52
name: Hero: Warrior: Yep, that's a cow all right.
text: Yep, that's a cow all right.

internal_name: PS_WARR53
name: Hero: Warrior: Too heavy.
text: Too heavy.

internal_name: PS_WARR54
name: Hero: Warrior: IN SPIRITU SANCTUM
text: IN SPIRITU SANCTUM

internal_name: PS_WARR55
name: Hero: Warrior: Predictum Oteum.
text: Predictum Oteum.

internal_name: PS_WARR56
name: Hero: Warrior: Ephesio orbitus ut inimicus.
text: Ephesio orbitus ut inimicus.

internal_name: PS_WARR57
name: Hero: Warrior: The enchantment is gone.
text: The enchantment is gone.

internal_name: PS_WARR58
name: Hero: Warrior: All too easy.
text: All too easy.

internal_name: PS_WARR59
name: Hero: Warrior: Back to the grave.
text: Back to the grave.

internal_name: PS_WARR60
name: Hero: Warrior: Time to die.
text: Time to die.

internal_name: PS_WARR61
name: Hero: Warrior: I'm not impressed.
text: I'm not impressed.

internal_name: PS_WARR62
name: Hero: Warrior: I'm sorry, did I break your concentration?
text: I'm sorry, did I break your concentration?

internal_name: PS_WARR63
name: Hero: Warrior: Vengeance is mine.
text: Vengeance is mine.

internal_name: PS_WARR64
name: Hero: Warrior: Die.
text: Die.

internal_name: PS_WARR65
name: Hero: Warrior: Yeah.
text: Yeah.

internal_name: PS_WARR66
name: Hero: Warrior: AHHHHHHHHH
text: AHHHHHHHHH

internal_name: PS_WARR67
name: Hero: Warrior: Whew!
text: Whew!

internal_name: PS_WARR68
name: Hero: Warrior: Ah!
text: Ah!

internal_name: PS_WARR69
name: Hero: Warrior: Ah!
text: Ah!

internal_name: PS_WARR70
name: Hero: Warrior: UGH!
text: UGH!

internal_name: PS_WARR71
name: Hero: Warrior: Oh, ah.
text: Oh, ah.

internal_name: PS_WARR72
name: Hero: Warrior: *crying*
text: *crying*

internal_name: PS_WARR73
name: Hero: Warrior: Ooooooh.
text: Ooooooh.

internal_name: PS_WARR74
name: Hero: Warrior: Whoa.
text: Whoa.

internal_name: PS_WARR75
name: Hero: Warrior: Thank the light.
text: Thank the light.

internal_name: PS_WARR76
name: Hero: Warrior: What was that?
text: What was that?

internal_name: PS_WARR77
name: Hero: Warrior: Hmm?
text: Hmm?

internal_name: PS_WARR78
name: Hero: Warrior: Hmm.
text: Hmm.

internal_name: PS_WARR79
name: Hero: Warrior: Uh-huh.
text: Uh-huh.

internal_name: PS_WARR80
name: Hero: Warrior: The spirits of the dead are now avenged.
text: The spirits of the dead are now avenged.

internal_name: PS_WARR81
name: Hero: Warrior: The town is safe from these foul spawn.
text: The town is safe from these foul spawn.

internal_name: PS_WARR82
name: Hero: Warrior: Rest well, Leoric. I'll find your son.
text: Rest well, Leoric. I'll find your son.

internal_name: PS_WARR83
name: Hero: Warrior: Your madness ends here, betrayer.
text: Your madness ends here, betrayer.

internal_name: PS_WARR84
name: Hero: Warrior: You'll lure no more men to their deaths.
text: You'll lure no more men to their deaths.

internal_name: PS_WARR85
name: Hero: Warrior: Return to heaven, warrior of light.
text: Return to heaven, warrior of light.

internal_name: PS_WARR86
name: Hero: Warrior: I can see why they fear this weapon.
text: I can see why they fear this weapon.

internal_name: PS_WARR87
name: Hero: Warrior: This must be what Griswold wanted.
text: This must be what Griswold wanted.

internal_name: PS_WARR88
name: Hero: Warrior: I need to get this to Lock Donnen.
text: I need to get this to Lock Donnen.

internal_name: PS_WARR89
name: Hero: Warrior: I need to get this to Griswold.
text: I need to get this to Griswold.

internal_name: PS_WARR90
name: Hero: Warrior: I've never been here before.
text: I've never been here before.

internal_name: PS_WARR91
name: Hero: Warrior: May the spirit of Arcane protect me.
text: May the spirit of Arcane protect me.

internal_name: PS_WARR92
name: Hero: Warrior: This is a place of great power.
text: This is a place of great power.

internal_name: PS_WARR93
name: Hero: Warrior: This blade must be destroyed.
text: This blade must be destroyed.

internal_name: PS_WARR94
name: Hero: Warrior: Your reign of pain has ended.
text: Your reign of pain has ended.

internal_name: PS_WARR95
name: Hero: Warrior: Now that's one big mushroom.
text: Now that's one big mushroom.

internal_name: PS_WARR99
name: Hero: Warrior: I must be getting close.
text: I must be getting close.

internal_name: USFX_IZUAL1
name: Izual: How much suffering, mortal, does it take before you lose your...
text: How much suffering, mortal, does it take before you lose your grace? Let me show you.

internal_name: USFX_LACH1
name: Lachdanan: Please, don't kill me, just hear me out. I was once captain o...
text: Please, don't kill me, just hear me out. I was once captain of King Leoric's knights, upholding the laws of this land with justice and honor. Then his dark curse fell upon us for the role we played in his tragic death. As my fellow knights succumbed to their twisted fate, I fled from the king's burial chamber, searching for some way to free myself from the curse. I failed. I heard of a golden elixir that could lift the curse and allow my soul to rest, but I have been unable to find it. My strength now wanes, and with it, the last of my humanity as well. Please, aid me and find the elixir. I will repay your efforts. I swear upon my honor.

internal_name: USFX_LACH2
name: Lachdanan: You have not found the golden elixir. I fear that I am doomed...
text: You have not found the golden elixir. I fear that I am doomed for eternity. Please, keep trying.

internal_name: USFX_LACH3
name: Lachdanan: You have saved my soul from damnation, and for that, I am in...
text: You have saved my soul from damnation, and for that, I am in your debt. If there is ever a way that I can repay you from beyond the grave, I will find it. But for now, take my helm. On the journey I'm about to take, I will have little use for it. May it protect you against the dark powers below. Go with the light, my friend. you

internal_name: PS_NAR1
name: Narrator: Take heed and bear witness to the truths that lie herein, for...
text: Take heed and bear witness to the truths that lie herein, for they are the last legacy of the Haradrim. There is a war that rages on even now, beyond the fields that we know, between the utopian kingdoms of the high heavens and the chaotic pits of the burning hells. This war is known as the Great Conflict, and it has raged and burned longer than any of the stars in the sky. Neither side ever gains sway for long, as the forces of light and darkness constantly vie for control over all creation.

internal_name: PS_NAR2
name: Narrator: Take heed and bear witness to the truths that lie herein, for...
text: Take heed and bear witness to the truths that lie herein, for they are the last legacy of the Herodrim. When the eternal conflict between the high heavens and the burning hells falls upon mortal soil, it is called the sin war. Angels and demons walk amongst humanity in disguise, fighting in secret away from the prying eyes of mortals. And help to dictate the course of the sin war.

internal_name: PS_NAR3
name: Narrator: Take heed and bear witness to the truths that lie herein, for...
text: Take heed and bear witness to the truths that lie herein, for they are the last legacy of the Haradrim. Nearly 300 years ago, it came to be known that the three prime evils of the burning hells had mysteriously come to our world. The three brothers ravaged the lands of the East for decades, while humanity was left trembling in their wake. Our order, the Haradrim, was founded by a group of secretive magi, to hunt down and capture the three evils once and for all. The original Haradrim captured two of the three within powerful artifacts known as soul stones and buried them deep beneath the desolate eastern sands. The third evil escaped capture and fled to the West with many of the Haradrim in pursuit. The third evil, known as Diablo, the Lord of Terror, was eventually captured. His essence set in a soul stone and buried within this labyrinth. Be warned that the soul stone must be kept from discovery by those not of the faith. If Diablo were to be released, he would seek a body that is easily controlled as he would be very weak, perhaps that of an old man or a child.

internal_name: PS_NAR4
name: Narrator: So it came to be that there was a great revolution within the...
text: So it came to be that there was a great revolution within the burning hells known as the Dark Exile. The lesser evils overthrew the three primevils and banished their spirit forms to the mortal realm. The demons Belial, the lord of lies, and Osmodan, the lord of sin, fought to claim rulership of hell during the absence of the three brothers. The factions of Belial and Osmodan, while the forces of the high heavens continually battered upon the very gates of hell.

internal_name: PS_NAR5
name: Narrator: Many demons traveled to the mortal realm in search of the thr...
text: Many demons traveled to the mortal realm in search of the three brothers. These demons were followed to the mortal plane by angels who hunted them throughout the vast cities of the east. The angels allied themselves with a secretive order of mortal magi, named the Haradrim, who quickly became adept at hunting demons. They also made many dark enemies in the underworlds.

internal_name: PS_NAR6
name: Narrator: So it came to be that the three primevils were banished in sp...
text: So it came to be that the three primevils were banished in spirit form to the mortal realm, and after sowing chaos across the east for decades, they were hunted down by the cursed order of the mortal Haradrim. The Haradrim used artifacts called soulstones to contain the essence of Mephisto, the lord of hatred, and his brother Baal, the lord of destruction. Eventually, the Haradrim captured Diablo within a soulstone as well and buried him under an ancient forgotten cathedral. There, the lord of terror sleeps and awaits the time of his rebirth. Know ye that he will seek a body of youth and power to possess, one that is innocent and easily controlled. And once more, fanned the flames of the sin war.

internal_name: PS_NAR7
name: Narrator: All praises to Diablo, lord of terror and survivor of the dar...
text: All praises to Diablo, lord of terror and survivor of the dark exile. When he awakened from his long slumber, my lord and master spoke to me of secrets that few mortals know. He told me the kingdoms of the high heavens and the pits of the burning hells engage in an eternal war. He revealed the powers that have brought this discord to the realms of man. My lord has named the battle for this world and all who exist here, the sin war.

internal_name: PS_NAR8
name: Narrator: Glory and approbation to Diablo, lord of terror and leader of...
text: Glory and approbation to Diablo, lord of terror and leader of the three. My lord spoke to me of his two brothers, Mephisto and Baal, who were banished to this world long ago. My lord wishes to bide his time and harness his awesome power so that he may free his captive brothers from their tombs beneath the sands of the east. Once my lord releases his brothers, the sin war will once again know the fury of the three.

internal_name: PS_NAR9
name: Narrator: Hail and sacrifice to Diablo, lord of terror and destroyer of...
text: Hail and sacrifice to Diablo, lord of terror and destroyer of souls. When I awoke my master from his sleep, he attempted to possess a mortal's form. Diablo attempted to claim the body of King Leoric, but my master was too weak from his imprisonment. My lord required a simple and innocent anchor to this world, and so found the boy Albrecht to be perfect for the task. While the good King Leoric was left maddened by Diablo's unsuccessful possession, I kidnapped his son Albrecht and brought him before my master. I now await Diablo's call and pray that I will be rewarded when he at last emerges as the lord of this world.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN0
name: Ogden: Thank goodness you've returned. Much has changed since you li...
text: Thank goodness you've returned. Much has changed since you lived here, my friend. All was peaceful until the dark riders came and destroyed our village. Many were cut down where they stood, and those who took up arms were slain or dragged away to become slaves, or worse. The church at the edge of town has been desecrated and is being used for dark rituals. The screams that echo in the night are inhuman, but some of our townsfolk may yet survive. Perhaps I can tell you more if we speak again. Good luck.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN1
name: Ogden: Lazarus was the archbishop who led many of the townspeople in...
text: Lazarus was the archbishop who led many of the townspeople into the labyrinth. I lost many good friends that day, and Lazarus never returned. I suppose he was killed along with most of the others. If you would do me a favor, good master, please do not talk to Farnam about that day.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN2
name: Ogden: I have always tried to keep a large supply of foodstuffs and...
text: I have always tried to keep a large supply of foodstuffs and drink in our storage cellar, but with the entire town having no source of fresh water, even our stores will soon run dry. Please, do what you can or I don't know what we will do.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN3
name: Ogden: That sounds quite disgusting, and I am afraid that I haven't...
text: That sounds quite disgusting, and I am afraid that I haven't heard anything about any worms. Perhaps Cain, the storyteller, could be of some help.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN4
name: Ogden: Jillian has been going on and on about strange lights in the...
text: Jillian has been going on and on about strange lights in the trees, but I haven't been able to make heads and tails of her story. I certainly haven't seen any strange lights, and if I did, they would be the least of my worries.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN5
name: Ogden: I am afraid that I don't know anything about that good master...
text: I am afraid that I don't know anything about that good master. Cain has many books that may be of some help.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN6
name: Ogden: These sound like dark creatures indeed. I am ignorant in matt...
text: These sound like dark creatures indeed. I am ignorant in matters of this nature, but I would assume that our storyteller may know of such legends.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN7
name: Ogden: There is an old story of an angel named Iswal, but I don't re...
text: There is an old story of an angel named Iswal, but I don't remember much more than that.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN8
name: Ogden: Yes, Farnam has mumbled something about a hulking brute who w...
text: Yes, Farnam has mumbled something about a hulking brute who wielded a fierce weapon. I believe he called him a butcher.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN9
name: Ogden: Wurt is talking backwards again? I hate it when he does that....
text: Wurt is talking backwards again? I hate it when he does that. I don't have time to help you decipher his riddle, but I will tell you one thing. Don't get involved with that rapscallion.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN10
name: Ogden: I never much cared for poetry. Occasionally I had calls to hi...
text: I never much cared for poetry. Occasionally I had calls to hire minstrels when the inn was doing well, but that seems like such a long time ago now. What? Oh, yes, well, I suppose you could see what someone else knows.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN11
name: Ogden: You speak of a brave warrior long dead. I'll have no such tal...
text: You speak of a brave warrior long dead. I'll have no such talk of speaking with departed souls in my in-yard, thank you very much.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN12
name: Ogden: Don't you think that Griswold would be a better person to ask...
text: Don't you think that Griswold would be a better person to ask about this? He's quite handy, you know.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN13
name: Ogden: Every child hears the story of the warrior Arcane and his mys...
text: Every child hears the story of the warrior Arcane and his mystic armor known as Valor. If you could find its resting place, you would be well protected against the evil in the labyrinth.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN14
name: Ogden: You know, sometimes I wonder how much faith you can put into...
text: You know, sometimes I wonder how much faith you can put into what Farnum says. He spends so much time reliving his memories of the labyrinth and just being plain drunk that he doesn't always make much sense. I guess you could ask around, though.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN15
name: Ogden: I saw the exorcism. It was incredible how Tremaine drove the...
text: I saw the exorcism. It was incredible how Tremaine drove the evil spirit from that man's wracked and tortured body. I pray that something that horrific never happens to anyone here ever again.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN16
name: Ogden: I'm afraid that I haven't heard anything about such a vicious...
text: I'm afraid that I haven't heard anything about such a vicious warrior, good master. I hope that you do not have to fight him, for he sounds extremely dangerous.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN17
name: Ogden: I'll bet that Wurt saw you coming and put on an act just so h...
text: I'll bet that Wurt saw you coming and put on an act just so he could laugh at you later when you're running around the town with your nose in the dirt. I'd ignore it.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN18
name: Ogden: The caravan stopped here to take on some supplies for their j...
text: The caravan stopped here to take on some supplies for their journey to the east. I sold them quite an array of fresh fruits and some excellent sweetbreads that Garda had just finished baking. Shame what happened to them.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN19
name: Ogden: Let me just say this. Both Garda and I would never, ever serv...
text: Let me just say this. Both Garda and I would never, ever serve black mushrooms to our honored guests. If Adria wants some mushrooms in her stew, then that is her business. But I can't help you find any black mushrooms. Disgusting.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN20
name: Ogden: If the witch can't help you and suggest that you see Cain, wh...
text: If the witch can't help you and suggest that you see Cain, what makes you think that I would know anything? It sounds like this is a very serious matter. You should hurry along and see the storyteller, as Adria suggests.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN21
name: Ogden: The village needs your help, good master. Some months ago, Ki...
text: The village needs your help, good master. Some months ago, King Leoric's son, Prince Albrecht, was kidnapped. The king went into a rage and scoured the village for his missing child. With each passing day, Leoric seemed to slip deeper into madness. He sought to blame innocent townsfolk for the boy's disappearance and had them brutally executed. Less than half of us survived his insanity. The king's knights and priests tried to placate him, but he turned against them and, sadly, to kill him. With his dying breath, the king called down a terrible curse upon his former followers. He vowed that they would serve him in darkness forever. This is where things take an even darker twist than I thought possible. Our former king has risen from his eternal sleep and now commands a legion of undead minions within the labyrinth. His body was buried in a tomb three levels beneath the cathedral. Please, good master, put his soul at ease by destroying his now cursed form.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN22
name: Ogden: As I told you, good master, the king was entombed three level...
text: As I told you, good master, the king was entombed three levels below. He's down there, waiting in the putrid darkness for his chance to destroy this land.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN23
name: Ogden: The curse of our king is past, but I fear that it was only pa...
text: The curse of our king is past, but I fear that it was only part of a greater evil at work. However, we may yet be saved from the darkness that consumes our land, for your victory is a good omen. May light guide you on your way, good master.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN24
name: Ogden: Master, I have a strange experience to relate. I know that yo...
text: Master, I have a strange experience to relate. I know that you have a great knowledge of those monstrosities that inhabit the labyrinth, and this is something that I cannot understand for the very life of me. I was awakened during the night by a scraping sound just outside of my tavern. When I looked out from my bedroom, I saw the shapes of small demon-like creatures in the inn yard. After a short time they ran off, but not before stealing the sign to my inn. I don't know why the demons would steal my sign, but leave my family in peace. It is strange now.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN25
name: Ogden: Oh, we didn't have to bring back my sign, but I suppose that...
text: Oh, we didn't have to bring back my sign, but I suppose that it does save me the expense of having another one made. Well, let me see. What could I give you as a fee for finding it? Hmm, what have we here? Oh, yes, this cap was left in one of the rooms by a magician who stayed here some time ago. Perhaps it may be of some value to you.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN26
name: Ogden: Your brave tales of fighting demons have reminded me of somet...
text: Your brave tales of fighting demons have reminded me of something, good master. A traveler passed through here some time ago. He was quite proud of a very unique weapon he held, and while becoming quite drunk, boasted of its power. I never saw him again, and I suspect that he ventured too close to the cathedral.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN27
name: Ogden: Have you ever seen that traveler I told you about? The one wi...
text: Have you ever seen that traveler I told you about? The one with the enchanted weapon? Well, I suppose that he left our village as so many others have. Or he must be dead.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN28
name: Ogden: Yes, that is certainly the weapon that he wore. You know, I'v...
text: Yes, that is certainly the weapon that he wore. You know, I've been thinking about something else that Traveller said. He inferred that the true powers of the weapon would be unleashed only when it tasted the blood of a very specific kind of creature.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN29
name: Ogden: Were the stories the traveler told us true? Oh, I see you don...
text: Were the stories the traveler told us true? Oh, I see you don't know yet. Well, I clearly recall that he said by slaying a certain monster, the weapon you found would become something quite special.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN30
name: Ogden: While I understand that your purpose may be of a higher calli...
text: While I understand that your purpose may be of a higher calling, surely some well-earned gold would be welcomed. Some townspeople from a nearby village have offered a reward for the destruction of a creature that raised their homes and property. They demand positive proof that the creature has been slain, and I can only think of one way to do that.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN31
name: Ogden: You can say whatever you want, but without proof I cannot giv...
text: You can say whatever you want, but without proof I cannot give you the reward.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN32
name: Ogden: Oh, disgusting, but certainly proof enough for anyone. Here's...
text: Oh, disgusting, but certainly proof enough for anyone. Here's reward as promised.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN33
name: Ogden: Good master, a moment of your time, please. My tavern was bro...
text: Good master, a moment of your time, please. My tavern was broken into during the night. No one was hurt, but many items were stolen, including a chest belonging to a mysterious wanderer who once stayed here. I found the body of a thief near the cathedral with telltale wounds from one of the creatures below marking his broken body. Some of the stolen goods were near the body, but the chest and the key to open it were nowhere in sight. Recover them. Then, if you find the chest, you can open it and see what secrets it contains. Perhaps it will be something that can help you on your quests.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN34
name: Ogden: Remember, good master, the chest is locked and is useless wit...
text: Remember, good master, the chest is locked and is useless without the key. If you do find the chest and get the key, you should see what's inside. I don't expect the owner back here again.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN35
name: Ogden: I see that you have found the key. Now you just need to find...
text: I see that you have found the key. Now you just need to find the chest that it belongs to.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN36
name: Ogden: Greetings, Good Master. Welcome to the Tavern of the Rising Sun.
text: Greetings, Good Master. Welcome to the Tavern of the Rising Sun.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN37
name: Ogden: Many adventurers have graced the tables of my tavern, and ten...
text: Many adventurers have graced the tables of my tavern, and ten times as many stories have been told over as much ale. The only thing that I ever heard any of them agree on was this old axiom. Perhaps it will help you. You can cut the flesh, but you must crush the bone.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN38
name: Ogden: Griswold the blacksmith is extremely knowledgeable about weap...
text: Griswold the blacksmith is extremely knowledgeable about weapons and armor. If you ever need work done on your gear, he is definitely the man to see.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN39
name: Ogden: Farnam spends far too much time here drowning his sorrows in...
text: Farnam spends far too much time here drowning his sorrows in cheap ale. I would make him leave, but he did suffer so during his time in the labyrinth.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN40
name: Ogden: Adria is wise beyond her years, but I must admit, she frighte...
text: Adria is wise beyond her years, but I must admit, she frightens me a little. Well, no matter. If you ever have need to trade in items of sorcery, she maintains a strangely well-stocked hut just across the river.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN41
name: Ogden: If you want to know more about the history of our village, th...
text: If you want to know more about the history of our village, the storyteller Kane knows quite a bit about the past.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN42
name: Ogden: The priest Tremaine is a bit of a mystery. He certainly never...
text: The priest Tremaine is a bit of a mystery. He certainly never stays here and he often comes and goes to many of the nearby towns.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN43
name: Ogden: Wirt is a rapscallion and a little scoundrel. He was always g...
text: Wirt is a rapscallion and a little scoundrel. He was always getting into trouble, and it's no surprise what happened to him. He probably went fooling about someplace that he shouldn't have been. I feel sorry for the boy, but I don't abide the company that he keeps.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN44
name: Ogden: Pepin is a good man, and certainly the most generous in the v...
text: Pepin is a good man, and certainly the most generous in the village. He's always attending to the needs of others, but trouble of some sort or another does seem to follow him wherever he goes.

internal_name: TSFX_TAVERN45
name: Ogden: Jillian, my barmaid? If it were not for her sense of duty to...
text: Jillian, my barmaid? If it were not for her sense of duty to her grandam, she would have fled from here long ago. Goodness knows I begged her to leave, telling her that I would watch after the old woman, but she is too sweet and caring to have done so.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER1
name: Pepin: The loss of his son was too much for King Leoric. I did what...
text: The loss of his son was too much for King Leoric. I did what I could to ease his madness, but in the end, it overcame him. A black curse has hung over this kingdom from that day forward, but perhaps if you were to free his spirit from his earthly prison, the curse would be lifted.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER2
name: Pepin: My goodness, demons running about the village at night, pilla...
text: My goodness, demons running about the village at night, pillaging our homes, is nothing sacred? I hope that Ogden and Garda are all right. I suppose that they would come to see me if they were hurt.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER3
name: Pepin: I was shocked when I heard of what the townspeople were plann...
text: I was shocked when I heard of what the townspeople were planning to do that night. I thought that of all people, Lazarus would have had more sense than that. He was an archbishop and always seemed to care so much for the townsfolk of Tristram. So many were injured, I could not save them all.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER4
name: Pepin: Ruf and Aeneas are missing? Light protect us. Is there no pla...
text: Ruf and Aeneas are missing? Light protect us. Is there no place that is safe? Our only hope of returning to a peaceful life rests in you. Please, you must find those boys and bring them home to their family.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER5
name: Pepin: This sounds like a very dangerous place. If you venture there...
text: This sounds like a very dangerous place. If you venture there, please take great care.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER6
name: Pepin: Horazon was insane. There are forces with which one does not...
text: Horazon was insane. There are forces with which one does not interfere. It would not surprise me if you found only the charred remains of this damned fool.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER7
name: Pepin: Farnam is often confused, but he speaks a powerful name when...
text: Farnam is often confused, but he speaks a powerful name when the word Iswal passes his lips. Cain would be able to tell you in much greater detail the legend of this warrior.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER8
name: Pepin: By the light, I know of this vile demon. There were many that...
text: By the light, I know of this vile demon. There were many that bore the scars of his wrath upon their bodies when the few survivors of the charge led by Lazarus crawled from the cathedral. I don't know what he used to slice open his victims, but it could not have been of this world. It left wounds festering with disease, and even I found them almost impossible to treat. Beware if you plan to battle this fiend.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER9
name: Pepin: I suppose it isn't beyond the realm of possibility if you cou...
text: I suppose it isn't beyond the realm of possibility if you could bear being in that room again. Your description of the atrocities committed there would be enough to keep me far from it.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER10
name: Pepin: This does seem familiar somehow. I seem to recall reading som...
text: This does seem familiar somehow. I seem to recall reading something very much like that poem while researching the history of demonic afflictions. It spoke of a place of great evil that... Wait, you're not going there, are you?

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER11
name: Pepin: A golden elixir, you say? I have never concocted a potion of...
text: A golden elixir, you say? I have never concocted a potion of that color before, so I can't tell you how it would affect you if you were to try to drink it. As your healer, I strongly advise that should you find such an elixir, do as Lockdownen asks, and do not try to use it.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER12
name: Pepin: If you had been looking for information on the Pestle of Curi...
text: If you had been looking for information on the Pestle of Curing or the Silver Chalice of Purification, I could have assisted you, my friend. However, in this matter, you would be better served to speak to either Griswold or Cain.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER13
name: Pepin: Hmm, it sounds like something I should remember, but I've bee...
text: Hmm, it sounds like something I should remember, but I've been so busy learning new cures and creating better elixirs that I must have forgotten. Sorry.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER14
name: Pepin: For once, I can vouch for Farnam's extraordinary claim. There...
text: For once, I can vouch for Farnam's extraordinary claim. There are many mentions in the books that I've been reading about a place of great healing where warriors of light would go to mend the wounds sustained in the Sin War. If you could find this place, it would most assuredly be to the benefit of us all.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER15
name: Pepin: I was asked to assist in the exorcism. My skills were able to...
text: I was asked to assist in the exorcism. My skills were able to ease the poor man's suffering as Tremaine drove the demon from his body. While I was treating him for an exceptionally high fever, he spoke of a place of searing heat. The tortured fellow cried out about hell and falling into a pit of flame. I could not make any sense of it, and thankfully he soon recovered.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER16
name: Pepin: Cain would be able to tell you much more about something like...
text: Cain would be able to tell you much more about something like this than I would ever wish to know.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER17
name: Pepin: I really don't have time to discuss some map you are looking...
text: I really don't have time to discuss some map you are looking for. I have many sick people that require my help, and yours as well.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER18
name: Pepin: I don't know what it is they thought they could see with that...
text: I don't know what it is they thought they could see with that rock, but I will say this. If rocks are falling from the sky, you would better be careful.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER19
name: Pepin: I can't make much of the writing on this map, but perhaps Adr...
text: I can't make much of the writing on this map, but perhaps Adria or Cain could help you decipher what this refers to. I can see that it is a map of the stars in our sky, but any more than that is beyond my talents.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER20
name: Pepin: I'm glad I caught up to you in time. Our wells have become br...
text: I'm glad I caught up to you in time. Our wells have become brackish and stagnant, and some of the townspeople have become ill drinking from them. Our reserves of fresh water are quickly running dry. I believe that there is a passage that leads to the springs that serve our town. Please find what has caused this calamity, or we all will surely perish.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER21
name: Pepin: Please, you must hurry. Every hour that passes brings us clos...
text: Please, you must hurry. Every hour that passes brings us closer to having no water to drink. We cannot survive for long without your help.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER22
name: Pepin: What's that you say? The mere presence of the demons has caus...
text: What's that you say? The mere presence of the demons has caused the water to become tainted? Oh, truly a great evil lurks beneath our town, but your perseverance and courage gives us hope. Please, take this ring. Perhaps it will aid you in the destruction of such vile creatures.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER23
name: Pepin: Good hero, a moment of your time, please. While attending one...
text: Good hero, a moment of your time, please. While attending one of the townsfolk who had taken quite ill, I noticed something odd about his home. There were strange sounds and a sickly sweet smell rising from the cellar. Thinking perhaps these fumes had something to do with his sickness, I investigated. In his cellar were monstrous worms shifting and squirming up from the underground. And make their way into the town. I left the door to his house open for you. It is the one opposite of mine.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER24
name: Pepin: I fear that the worms could soon overrun the village. I know...
text: I fear that the worms could soon overrun the village. I know that they are coming up from under the house that is opposite mine. Just the thought of those slimy beasts oozing into my house makes me want to be ill. Please, rid us of them.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER25
name: Pepin: Once again you have saved this humble town from the encroachi...
text: Once again you have saved this humble town from the encroaching evil. We are, as always, forever in your debt.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER26
name: Pepin: The witch told me that you were searching for the brain of a...
text: The witch told me that you were searching for the brain of a demon to assist me in creating my elixir. It should be of great value to the many who were injured by those foul beasts if I can just unlock the secrets I suspect that its alchemy holds. If you can remove the brain of a demon when you kill it, I would be grateful if you could bring it to me.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER27
name: Pepin: Excellent! This is just what I had in mind. I was able to fin...
text: Excellent! This is just what I had in mind. I was able to finish the elixir without this, but it can't hurt to have this to study. Would you please carry this to the witch? I believe that she is expecting it.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER28
name: Pepin: My friend, I must speak with you. While going to help a sick...
text: My friend, I must speak with you. While going to help a sick villager, I came upon a demon in the town. I fled from the house and accidentally left the door open in my haste. I pray that the vile creature is still in there. Please, help us before it comes for us all.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER29
name: Pepin: These creatures must be banished from our town. To my shame,...
text: These creatures must be banished from our town. To my shame, I left the door open, but that should make it all the easier for you to find the house.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER30
name: Pepin: Once again, the town is in your debt. It is only your strengt...
text: Once again, the town is in your debt. It is only your strength and force of will that can lead us out of this evil time.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER31
name: Pepin: Once again, I require your strong arm and quick wits to aid t...
text: Once again, I require your strong arm and quick wits to aid the people of this town. I am in need of certain reagents to help fight the plagues that the demons have unleashed on the land by their very presence. If you could gather these few items, it will save many lives.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER32
name: Pepin: The disease is spread quickly and many are dying. Please help...
text: The disease is spread quickly and many are dying. Please help me by finding the reagents so that I can use them to make an antidote.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER33
name: Pepin: Thank you so much. You bring hope and light to these dark and...
text: Thank you so much. You bring hope and light to these dark and troubled times. I wish for you to have this in the hopes that it will aid you in your battle against the darkness.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER34
name: Pepin: I know that I ask much of you, but I must now ask that you fi...
text: I know that I ask much of you, but I must now ask that you find a pool of clear water. Take these containers, fill them, and return them to me as soon as you can. With the clear water, I can create an elixir of wondrous power that will benefit us all.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER35
name: Pepin: Have you brought what I need? The clear water will allow me t...
text: Have you brought what I need? The clear water will allow me to create a very powerful elixir. Fill the containers that I gave you and return with them.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER36
name: Pepin: Very good, my friend. Very good! Just give me a minute to mix...
text: Very good, my friend. Very good! Just give me a minute to mix these ingredients. Perfect! Here are some of the elixir, as promised.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER37
name: Pepin: What ails you, my friend?
text: What ails you, my friend?

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER38
name: Pepin: I have made a very interesting discovery. Unlike us, the crea...
text: I have made a very interesting discovery. Unlike us, the creatures in the labyrinth can heal themselves without the aid of potions or magic. If you hurt one of the monsters, make sure it is dead, or it very well may regenerate itself.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER39
name: Pepin: Before it was taken over by, well, whatever looks below, the...
text: Before it was taken over by, well, whatever looks below, the cathedral was a place of great learning. There are many books to be found there. If you find any, you should read them all, for some may hold secrets to the workings of the labyrinth.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER40
name: Pepin: Griswold knows as much about the art of war as I do about the...
text: Griswold knows as much about the art of war as I do about the art of healing. He is a shrewd merchant, but his work is second to none. Oh, I suppose that may be because he's the only blacksmith left here.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER41
name: Pepin: Cain is a true friend and a wise sage. He maintains a vast li...
text: Cain is a true friend and a wise sage. He maintains a vast library and has an innate ability to discern the true nature of many things. If you ever have any questions, he is the person to go to.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER42
name: Pepin: Even my skills have been unable to fully heal Farnum. Oh, I h...
text: Even my skills have been unable to fully heal Farnum. Oh, I have been able to mend his body, but his mind and spirit are beyond anything I can do.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER43
name: Pepin: While I use some limited forms of magic to create the potions...
text: While I use some limited forms of magic to create the potions and elixirs I store here, Adria is a true sorceress. She never seems to sleep, and she always has access to many mystic tomes and artifacts. I believe her hut may be much more than the hovel it appears to be, but I can never seem to get inside the place.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER44
name: Pepin: His holiness is a wondrous man of great knowledge and underst...
text: His holiness is a wondrous man of great knowledge and understanding. He has shown me many cures for rare and deadly diseases. He brings me books and reagents for my work whenever he can, but I fear that he may someday take on some task that is too great even for him.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER45
name: Pepin: Poor Wirt. I did all that was possible for the child, but I k...
text: Poor Wirt. I did all that was possible for the child, but I know he despises that wooden peg that I was forced to attach to his leg. His wounds were hideous. No one, and especially such a young child, should have to suffer the way he did.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER46
name: Pepin: I really don't understand why Ogden stays here in Tristram. H...
text: I really don't understand why Ogden stays here in Tristram. He suffers from a slight nervous condition, but he is an intelligent and industrious man who would do very well wherever he went. I suppose it may be the fear of the many murders that happen in the surrounding countryside, or perhaps the wishes of his wife that keep him and his family where they are.

internal_name: TSFX_HEALER47
name: Pepin: Ogden's barmaid is a sweet girl. Her grandmother is quite ill...
text: Ogden's barmaid is a sweet girl. Her grandmother is quite ill and suffers from delusions. She claims that they are visions, but I have no proof of that one way or the other.

internal_name: IS_QUESTDN
name: Quest Done: you
text: you

internal_name: IS_SARC
name: Sarcophagus: *Burr*
text: *Burr*

internal_name: USFX_SKING1
name: Skeleton King: The warmth of life has entered my tomb. Prepare yourself, mor...
text: The warmth of life has entered my tomb. Prepare yourself, mortal, to serve my master for eternity.

internal_name: USFX_SNOT1
name: Snotspill: Hey! You that one that kill all! You get me magic banner, or...
text: Hey! You that one that kill all! You get me magic banner, or we attack! You now live with life! You kill big ugly and give back magic! Go past corner and door, find ugly! You give, you go!

internal_name: USFX_SNOT2
name: Snotspill: You kill uglies! Get banger! You bring to me or else!
text: You kill uglies! Get banger! You bring to me or else!

internal_name: USFX_SNOT3
name: Snotspill: You give? Yes, good! Go now! Which turn? We kill all with big...
text: You give? Yes, good! Go now! Which turn? We kill all with big magic!

internal_name: USFX_CLEAVER
name: The Butcher: Ah, fresh meat.
text: Ah, fresh meat.

internal_name: TSFX_PRIEST0
name: Tremain the Priest: All I can do now is pray for us all.
text: All I can do now is pray for us all.

internal_name: TSFX_PRIEST1
name: Tremain the Priest: I seek a champion to undertake a serious duty, and the people...
text: I seek a champion to undertake a serious duty, and the people of this town speak well of your courage and skill. The Archbishop Lazarus, once King Leoric's most trusted advisor and a member of our order, has taken the path of evil. Not long ago, Lazarus led a party of simple townsfolk into the labyrinth to find the king's missing son, Albrecht. Only a few of them escaped with their lives. Fool! I should have suspected his veiled treachery then, for I have learned that it was Lazarus himself who kidnapped Leoric's son and has since hidden him within the labyrinth. I still don't understand why the Archbishop has turned to the darkness, or what his interest is in Albrecht. Unless he means to sacrifice him at the full moon. That must be what he has planned. The survivors of his rescue party, say that Lazarus was last seen in the deepest bowels of the labyrinth, some sixteen levels beneath the cathedral. You must hurry and save the prince from the sacrificial blade of this demented fiend.

internal_name: TSFX_PRIEST2
name: Tremain the Priest: Why do you delay? Time is of the essence. The prince and the...
text: Why do you delay? Time is of the essence. The prince and the people of this kingdom are counting on you.

internal_name: TSFX_PRIEST3
name: Tremain the Priest: So, Lazarus has paid the price for his betrayal, and justice...
text: So, Lazarus has paid the price for his betrayal, and justice is served. For your services this day, I bestow this mace unto you. Its name is Lightforge, and it is the holiest of our Order's artifacts. As I am the last of this Order, I entrust it to you. May the Light guide you.

internal_name: TSFX_PRIEST4
name: Tremain the Priest: This is terrible. Lazarus will surely burn in hell for his ho...
text: This is terrible. Lazarus will surely burn in hell for his horrific deed. Although the boy that you describe may not be our prince, I believe that Albrecht may yet be in danger. Whatever vile power lies beneath the ground has assuredly secured its foothold in our world. All I can do now is pray for us all.

internal_name: TSFX_PRIEST5
name: Tremain the Priest: I have had a most disturbing experience that I must share wit...
text: I have had a most disturbing experience that I must share with you, my friend. Earlier today, I was called upon to help one of the men that escaped from the labyrinth. He was deranged, violent, and kept lashing out at all of those who tried to calm him. I suspected that he was possessed by some sort of demonic entity, and so began to drive the evil from within him. After many hours, I was able to exorcise a demon who called himself Fleshdoom, but the hellion fled into the labyrinth. You may think that I am mad, but after speaking with the man and battling with Fleshdoom, I believe that the labyrinth has somehow become a gateway to the underworld. As you descend deeper, you may find yourself upon the doorstep of hell itself. Finally, the man who was possessed retained memories of an ancient demon blade named Shadowfang. The man who was possessed by the devil's sword. While I fear the dangers below grow even greater, you must find Fleshdoom and slay him. Bring the sword to me and I can destroy it, but do not wield it, for its power can corrupt absolutely.

internal_name: TSFX_PRIEST6
name: Tremain the Priest: Flesh Dome's demise is a great good to the world, yet Shadowf...
text: Flesh Dome's demise is a great good to the world, yet Shadowfang remains. It must be found and destroyed. Do not attempt to use the Demon Blade, champion. It will corrupt and madden any mortal who wields it. I alone can end its dark evil.

internal_name: TSFX_PRIEST7
name: Tremain the Priest: Light be praised! You've found the cursed demon blade! Only i...
text: Light be praised! You've found the cursed demon blade! Only its destruction can ensure the safety of us all! Wait! What treachery is this? Ah! It burns! Hellfire! Consuming me! You must take this to the Hellforge and cast it in before a... No!

internal_name: USFX_WLOCK1
name: Warlock: Mortal, free me from my imprisonment and your reward will be...
text: Mortal, free me from my imprisonment and your reward will be more than you can imagine. Read the book and I will be released.

internal_name: USFX_WARLRD1
name: Warlord of Blood: My blade sings for your blood, mortal. And by my dark masters...
text: My blade sings for your blood, mortal. And by my dark masters it shall not be denied.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY1
name: Wirt: Look, I'm running a business here. I don't sell information,...
text: Look, I'm running a business here. I don't sell information, and I don't care about some king that's been dead longer than I've been alive. If you need something to use against this king of the undead, then I can help you out.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY2
name: Wirt: What? Is he saying I took that? I suppose that Griswold is on...
text: What? Is he saying I took that? I suppose that Griswold is on his side too. Look, I got over simple sign stealing months ago. You can't turn a profit on a piece of wood.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY3
name: Wirt: Yes, the righteous Lazarus, who is so effective against those...
text: Yes, the righteous Lazarus, who is so effective against those monsters down there. Didn't help save my leg, did it? Look, I'll give you a free piece of advice. Ask Farnum. He was there.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY4
name: Wirt: For once, I'm with you. My business runs dry, so to speak, if...
text: For once, I'm with you. My business runs dry, so to speak, if I have no market to sell to. You better find out what is going on, and soon.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY5
name: Wirt: They have you hunting worms now? What's next? Leaf collecting...
text: They have you hunting worms now? What's next? Leaf collecting? Picking up mushrooms? Look, friend, you have a whole church full of demons over there to worry about. I don't see how a few little worms could be so bad.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY6
name: Wirt: You know, I've been looking for those lights, but I can't fin...
text: You know, I've been looking for those lights, but I can't find them. If Jillian says they are there, I believe her, but I have yet to see them for myself.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY7
name: Wirt: A vast and mysterious treasure, you say? Maybe I could be int...
text: A vast and mysterious treasure, you say? Maybe I could be interested in picking up a few things from you. Or better yet, don't you need some rare and expensive supplies to get you through this ordeal?

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY8
name: Wirt: The care and feeding of demons is definitely not an interest...
text: The care and feeding of demons is definitely not an interest of mine. Here is a piece of friendly advice. If you get the chance, kill anything you see down there.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY9
name: Wirt: If you were to find any trace of Iswal or the Blade Azurath,...
text: If you were to find any trace of Iswal or the Blade Azurath, even I would be impressed. That is definitely one of a kind.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY10
name: Wirt: I know more than you think about that grizzly fiend. His litt...
text: I know more than you think about that grizzly fiend. His little friends got a hold of me and managed to get my leg before Griswold pulled me out of that hole. I'll put it bluntly. Kill him before he kills you and adds your corpse to his collection.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY11
name: Wirt: Let's see. Am I selling you something? No. Are you giving me...
text: Let's see. Am I selling you something? No. Are you giving me money to tell you about this? No. Are you now leaving and going to talk to the storyteller who lives for this kind of thing? Yes.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY12
name: Wirt: Wait, let me guess. Kane was swallowed up in a gigantic fissu...
text: Wait, let me guess. Kane was swallowed up in a gigantic fissure that opened beneath him. He was incinerated in a ball of hellfire and can't answer your questions anymore. Oh, that isn't what happened? Then I guess you'll be buying something, or you'll be on your way.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY13
name: Wirt: If you were to find this artifact for Griswold, it could put...
text: If you were to find this artifact for Griswold, it could put a serious damper on my business here. Ah, you'll never find it.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY14
name: Wirt: You intend to find the armor known as Valor? No one has ever...
text: You intend to find the armor known as Valor? No one has ever figured out where Arcane stashed the stuff. And if my contacts couldn't find it, I seriously doubt you ever will either.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY15
name: Wirt: This is one time that you should listen to Farnham. I have he...
text: This is one time that you should listen to Farnham. I have heard of this place, and I know a few sorcerers who have tried to create a portal to get there.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY16
name: Wirt: I don't know who this flesh doom is, but I have heard rumors...
text: I don't know who this flesh doom is, but I have heard rumors of an ebon blade that cleaves a soul from the body. Even I would not try to sell that thing, no matter what the profit. If you find it, you should do as Tremaine says, and destroy it as quickly as possible.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY17
name: Wirt: I haven't ever dealt with this warlord you speak of, but he s...
text: I haven't ever dealt with this warlord you speak of, but he sounds like he's going through a lot of swords. Wouldn't mind supplying his armies.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY18
name: Wirt: If anyone can make something out of that rock, Griswold can....
text: If anyone can make something out of that rock, Griswold can. He knows what he is doing. And as much as I try to steal his customers, I respect the quality of his work.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY19
name: Wirt: I don't have any mushrooms of any size or color for sale. How...
text: I don't have any mushrooms of any size or color for sale. How about something a bit more useful?

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY20
name: Wirt: I've been looking for a map, but that certainly isn't it. You...
text: I've been looking for a map, but that certainly isn't it. You should show that to Adria. She can probably tell you what it is. I'll say one thing. It looks old. And old usually means valuable.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY21
name: Wirt: Hear over, pssst! Chamber Butcher, the From Spell Portal, tow...
text: Hear over, pssst! Chamber Butcher, the From Spell Portal, town the cast! Saying, am I what C?

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY22
name: Wirt: Get out, it figured you haven't! Understand, could you even s...
text: Get out, it figured you haven't! Understand, could you even so simple it make to try die? Chamber butcher the From Spell Portal town the cast!

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY23
name: Wirt: Where is that stupid map? It was supposed to be between the r...
text: Where is that stupid map? It was supposed to be between the rock and the tree before the bridge. Should be right. Oh, hello there. Didn't see you standing there.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY24
name: Wirt: Rock? Tree? Bridge? I have no idea what you're talking about.
text: Rock? Tree? Bridge? I have no idea what you're talking about.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY25
name: Wirt: Look, I know my prices are high, but one of my contacts had a...
text: Look, I know my prices are high, but one of my contacts had an accident, and I need some help refilling my more mundane inventory. I'll trade you a quality item if you can just complete this little list for me.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY26
name: Wirt: Listen, I'll make it worth your time if you will get me what...
text: Listen, I'll make it worth your time if you will get me what I asked you for. Besides, you know you want to find out what I'm going to give you in return.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY27
name: Wirt: Thanks. This should hold me over until I can find a new erran...
text: Thanks. This should hold me over until I can find a new errand boy. Too bad you're so busy. Oh yeah, here's your part of the bargain.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY28
name: Wirt: Psst, over here. I have something very special for sale today...
text: Psst, over here. I have something very special for sale today. I'm not exactly sure what it is, but I can just tell that it's great. I'm gonna offer you a bargain. A thousand gold takes it. Right now, no questions and no returns.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY29
name: Wirt: Hey, you! Yeah, I'm talking to you. I acquired this strange b...
text: Hey, you! Yeah, I'm talking to you. I acquired this strange book. I know it must do something big, but you need a crystal eyepiece to read it, so it's useless to me. However, I would be willing to trade you this rare and mystical tome for just a few things.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY30
name: Wirt: Look, this very special book that I have can be yours for so...
text: Look, this very special book that I have can be yours for so little. Don't tell anyone what a great deal I'm giving you or it would ruin my reputation.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY31
name: Wirt: Amazing! You actually found everything I wanted. Well, here's...
text: Amazing! You actually found everything I wanted. Well, here's the book, but you're going to have to find a crystal eyepiece to read it. Good luck!

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY32
name: Wirt: Psst! Over here!
text: Psst! Over here!

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY33
name: Wirt: Not everyone in Tristram has a use or a market for everything...
text: Not everyone in Tristram has a use or a market for everything you'll find in the labyrinth. Not even me, as hard as that is to believe. Sometimes only you will be able to find a purpose for some things.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY34
name: Wirt: Don't trust everything the drunk says. Too many ales have fog...
text: Don't trust everything the drunk says. Too many ales have fogged his vision and his good sense.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY35
name: Wirt: In case you haven't noticed, I don't buy anything from Tristr...
text: In case you haven't noticed, I don't buy anything from Tristram. I am an importer of quality goods. If you want to peddle your junk, you'll have to see Griswold, Pepin, or that witch Adria. I'm sure they'll snap up whatever you can bring them.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY36
name: Wirt: I guess I owe the blacksmith my life. What there is of it. Su...
text: I guess I owe the blacksmith my life. What there is of it. Sure, Griswold offered me an apprenticeship at the smithy. He's a nice enough guy, but I'll never get enough money to... Well, let's just say that I have definite plans that require a large amount of gold.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY37
name: Wirt: If I were a few years older, I would shower her with whatever...
text: If I were a few years older, I would shower her with whatever riches I could muster. And let me assure you, I could get my hands on some very nice stuff. Jillian is a beautiful girl who should get out of Tristram as soon as it is safe. Hmm, maybe I'll take her with me when I go.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY38
name: Wirt: Kane knows too much. He scares the life out of me, even more...
text: Kane knows too much. He scares the life out of me, even more than that woman across the river. He keeps telling me about how lucky I am to be alive and how my story is foretold in legend. I think he's off his crock.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY39
name: Wirt: "Farnum, now there is a man with serious problems, and I know...
text: "Farnum, now there is a man with serious problems, and I know all about how serious problems can be. He trusted too much in the integrity of one man, and Lazarus led him into the very jaws of death. Oh, I know what it's like down there, so don't even start telling me about your plans to destroy the evil that dwells in that labyrinth. Just watch your legs.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY40
name: Wirt: As long as you don't need anything reattached, old Pepin is a...
text: As long as you don't need anything reattached, old Pepin is as good as they come. If I'd have had some of those potions he brews, I might still have my leg.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY41
name: Wirt: Yeah, Tremaine. He gets around, doesn't he? Or haven't you he...
text: Yeah, Tremaine. He gets around, doesn't he? Or haven't you heard? My friends in some of the other towns say that he passes through, picking up a few books here, a pinch of bat claw there. Never seems to have the problems most do getting in and out of Tristram, that's for sure.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY42
name: Wirt: Adria truly bothers me. Sure, Cain is creepy in what he can t...
text: Adria truly bothers me. Sure, Cain is creepy in what he can tell you about the past, but that witch can see into your past. She always has some way to get whatever she needs, too. Adria gets her hands on more merchandise than I've seen pass through the gates of the King's Bazaar during High Festival.

internal_name: TSFX_PEGBOY43
name: Wirt: Ogden is a fool for staying here. I could get him out of town...
text: Ogden is a fool for staying here. I could get him out of town for a very reasonable price, but he insists on trying to make a go of it with that stupid tavern. I guess at the least he gives Jillian a place to work, and his wife Garda does make a superb shepherd's pie.

internal_name: TSFX_DEADGUY
name: Wounded Townsman: Please help. I barely escaped from the butcher. He killed my...
text: Please help. I barely escaped from the butcher. He killed my wife, my children. I beg of you, in the name of God, avenge them.

internal_name: TSFX_WOUND
name: Wounded Townsman: Please, listen to me. The Archbishop Lazarus, he led us down...
text: Please, listen to me. The Archbishop Lazarus, he led us down here to find the lost prince. The bastard led us into a trap. Now everyone is dead, killed by a demon he called the Butcher. Avenge us! Find this butcher and slay him, so that our souls may finally rest.

internal_name: USFX_ZHAR1
name: Zhar the Mad: What? Why are you here? All these interruptions are enough to...
text: What? Why are you here? All these interruptions are enough to make one insane. Here, take this and leave me to my work. Trouble me no more.

internal_name: USFX_ZHAR2
name: Zhar the Mad: Your curiosity will be the death of you.
text: Your curiosity will be the death of you.
